md`# brain-dashboard

A Cloud Brain recipe: metrics read from the lines this Brain's Workers already log. A metric is a definition that names a Worker, the \`at\` of its lines, a numeric field to add up (or none: the lines are counted) and the fields a query may group or filter by. Nothing is added to the Worker that writes the lines. The metrics of the Brain's own Workers are a value of this module; a member's are rows of this service. A dashboard is data: a name, a title and a list of panels, each naming a metric and how it is drawn. Tasks 1 to 4 of \`plan/cloud-brain-dashboard-service.md\`; the page that draws a dashboard is a later task and is not here.

| Method | Answers |
|---|---|
| \`GET metric.list\` | \`{ metrics }\`: the definitions the caller may name, no data |
| \`GET metric.query?metric=NAME&since=MS&until=MS&by=dim,dim&DIM=value\` | \`{ metric, since, until, step, groups, sampled, series, cost }\`: one Cloudflare telemetry query (\`POST /accounts/ACCOUNT/workers/observability/telemetry/query\`, \`view: "calculations"\`), with one more for each day of a span that Cloudflare answered from a sample (A query), or the answer kept from those (What a query costs) |
| \`POST metric.put\` | a member's own. Body \`{ name, worker, at, value, dims }\`; answers \`{ metric }\`, the definition as kept. A name that is kept is written over |
| \`POST metric.delete\` | a member's own. Body \`{ name }\`; answers \`{ deleted }\`, or 404 for a name that is not kept |
| \`GET dashboard.list\` | \`{ dashboards }\`: \`{ name, title }\` of each dashboard the caller may read, no panels |
| \`GET dashboard.get?name=NAME\` | \`{ dashboard }\`: \`{ name, title, panels }\`, or 404 for a name that is not kept |
| \`POST dashboard.put\` | Body \`{ name, title, panels }\`; answers \`{ dashboard }\`, the dashboard as kept. A name that is kept is written over |
| \`POST dashboard.delete\` | Body \`{ name }\`; answers \`{ deleted }\`, or 404 for a name that is not kept |
| Storage | \`rows\`. Key \`metric/<name>\`: a member's definition, \`{ name, worker, at, value, dims }\`. Key \`dashboard/<name>\`: a dashboard, \`{ name, title, panels }\`. The member's DID is not kept |

## The metrics

The metrics of the Brain's own Workers are a value of this module (\`metricDefinitions\`) and no method writes one: adding one is a change to the seed.

| Name | Worker | Lines | Value | Dimensions |
|---|---|---|---|---|
${metricTable}

For a line of the deployer the Worker deployed is \`target\`; \`worker\` on it is the writer. The core's line also holds \`caller\`, \`holder\`, \`delegation\` and \`by\`, which are not dimensions and cannot be asked for.

## A query

\`since\` and \`until\` are times in milliseconds. Each is cut to the minute it is in (\`since=…12345\` is asked as the start of that minute), and the answer's \`since\` and \`until\` are the cut ones; \`since\` is in a minute before \`until\`'s, or the call is 400. With neither, the hour that ends at the start of this minute, and with \`until\` alone the hour before it (an \`until\` under an hour is 400). \`by\` is a list of dimensions of the metric, joined with commas. Any other parameter is a filter and its name is a dimension: \`target=brain-x-git\`, \`status=502\`. A name that is not a dimension of the metric is answered 400, in \`by\` or as a filter, and Cloudflare is not asked.

The caller sends no body of Cloudflare's. The service writes it (\`metricBody\`): the script of the definition's Worker (\`logsScope\` of brain-logs, with the Worker named), the line's \`at\`, the filters asked, \`groupBys\` of \`by\` with each dimension's type, a count, and for a metric with a value its sum and max; \`limit\` 500.

\`\`\`js
GET /xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.metric.query?metric=deploys.confirmed&by=target&since=1791676800000&until=1791680400000
{ "metric": "deploys.confirmed", "since": 1791676800000, "until": 1791680400000,
  "step": 60000,       // Cloudflare's result.run.granularity; the service does not choose it
  "groups": 2,         // how many groups Cloudflare answered; 500 or more means it cut the answer
  "sampled": 1,        // 1: counted from every line. More: Cloudflare counted from a sample, and n, sum and max are its estimates
  "series": [{ "t": 1791676860000, "target": "brain-x-git", "n": 2, "sum": null, "max": null }],
  "cost": { "ms": 431,           // from the send to Cloudflare until its whole answer was read; 0 from the memory (431 is an example, not a measure)
            "queries": 1,        // how many queries Cloudflare was sent for this answer: 1, 1 and the parts of a sampled span, or 0 from the memory
            "cached": false } }  // true: the answer is one kept in this instance's memory
\`\`\`

A row is one step and one group: \`t\` the step's time, the dimensions asked, \`n\` the lines, \`sum\` and \`max\` of the value (\`null\` for a counted metric). Steps with no line have no row. Cloudflare's refusal is answered 502 with its status in the message.

**An answer says whether Cloudflare made it from a sample of the lines: \`sampled\`.** \`1\` is an answer counted from every line. Above 1, each \`n\`, \`sum\` and \`max\` is Cloudflare's estimate from a sample, and a group with few lines can be left out whole. \`sampled\` is the highest of two numbers of Cloudflare's answer, either of which can be absent: \`result.run.statistics.abr_level\` ("The level of Adaptive Bit Rate (ABR) sampling used for the query. If empty the ABR level is 1") and the \`sampleInterval\` of each row ("A value above 1 means count and value are estimated from sampled data, not exact"). Both sentences are Cloudflare's, from its API reference of the telemetry query, read 2026-10-11. With neither number, \`sampled\` is 1.

**A sampled answer over more than a day is asked again a day at a time.** The service sends the span as one query. When that answer is sampled and the span is longer than ${metricPieceDefaults.ms / 3600000} hours, it sends one query for each part of ${metricPieceDefaults.ms / 3600000} hours, counted back from \`until\` so that the first part is the short one, all at the same moment, and answers the rows of the parts in place of the first answer. \`step\` is then the longest of the parts' steps, \`groups\` the most any part answered, \`sampled\` the highest of the parts' (1 when every part was whole), and \`cost.queries\` is 1 and the parts. An answer is given as it is, with its \`sampled\`, and nothing is asked again, for a span of ${metricPieceDefaults.ms / 3600000} hours or less and for a span of more than ${metricPieceDefaults.most} parts. A part ends at the time the next one starts; whether Cloudflare counts a line of that millisecond in both was not read. Cloudflare's refusal of a part is answered 502, as of the span, and nothing is kept. The setting \`pieceMs\` stands in for the ${metricPieceDefaults.ms} ms; \`0\` asks nothing again (\`config.set { worker: "brain-x-dashboard", key: "pieceMs", value: 0 }\`, the owner, no deploy; not run on a Brain).

What was counted on cb4 before this, 2026-10-11, with the service at \`f8667794afd8\`, which sent one query and read neither number: \`deploys.confirmed\` by \`target\`, against the lines \`at: "deploy.confirmed"\` that \`logs.deploys\` read over the same span, which are read whole:

| span | sum of \`n\` | the lines |
|---|---|---|
| 1 hour, 24 hours, 2 days, 3 days | 6, 62, 136, 171 | the same, target by target |
| 4 days, one ask | 160, over 7 targets | 173, over 22 targets |
| 5 days, 6 days, one ask each | 173, 173 | the same, target by target |
| 7 days, five asks of six | 160, over 7 targets | 173, over 22 targets |
| 7 days, the sixth ask | 100, one target | 173 |
| the same 7 days, seven asks of one day | 173 | the same, target by target |

In each of the seven answers that were short every \`n\` was a multiple of 10, and a target could be left out whole: \`brain-db\`, with 10 lines, was in none of them. The six 7-day asks differed by minutes at each end and held the same 173 lines. So the span alone does not say which answer is whole: 4 days was short where 5 and 6 were not, and \`groups\` does not show it (22 for the 4-day answer). That is why the service goes by what Cloudflare says of each answer and by no length of span. The asks are in \`tools/cloud-brain/records/dsv-4-cost.md\`.

## What a query costs

An answer is kept in the memory of the instance of the Worker that made it, for ${metricMemoryDefaults.ms / 1000} s from when Cloudflare answered, under the text of the query Cloudflare was sent (\`metricMemory\`). A span asked again in parts is kept as one answer, the joined one, under the text of the query for the span. The same query asked of that instance inside that time is answered from the memory: Cloudflare is sent nothing, and \`cost\` is \`{ "ms": 0, "queries": 0, "cached": true }\`. The rest of the answer is the kept one, so it can be ${metricMemoryDefaults.ms / 1000} s old. The minutes are what make two asks the same query: a page that asks "the last hour" again inside one minute sends the same text.

- **The same query** is the same metric, minutes, \`by\` in the same order and filters in the same order. Who asks is not part of it. Every refusal of this service is decided before the memory is read (the tenant, the definition, the names in \`by\` and the filters), so an answer kept for one caller is given to another only when the service would have asked Cloudflare for that caller too.
- **A member's metric put again** with another Worker, \`at\` or value, or another type of a dimension the query names, is another query. Deleted, it is 404.
- **Not kept:** Cloudflare's refusal (the next ask is sent again), and an answer that with its query is over ${metricMemoryDefaults.characters} characters. That number is also the most the memory holds; the oldest answer goes first.
- **Another instance has its own memory.** Cloudflare starts and ends instances of a Worker as it chooses, so a query asked again inside the time can be sent again. On cb4, 2026-10-11, 32 asks were made again up to 50 s after the answer, by one caller, one at a time: each was answered from the memory. The ask made 60 s after was sent again. An ask that reached an instance without the answer was not seen; how long an instance lives, and how many run at once, was not counted.
- **Two asks at the same moment** of a query that is not kept are each sent: an ask does not wait for another's. The memory is read before Cloudflare is asked and written after it answered (\`dashboard_service\`). On cb4, 2026-10-11: three pairs sent together, and each of the six answers had \`"cached": false\`.
- **The setting \`memoryMs\`** stands in for the ${metricMemoryDefaults.ms} ms; \`0\` keeps nothing. The owner, with no deploy: \`config.set { worker: "brain-x-dashboard", key: "memoryMs", value: 0 }\` (brain-core, Settings; not run on a Brain).

\`cost\` is this service's count of what the answer took from Cloudflare. It is not a price, and the core charges nothing for the call (No price, below). An answer from the memory is still a call to the core: its line is written, and a call sent by a member's Worker is counted against its author's calls for the day before this service is reached.

**Measured on cb4**, 2026-10-11 from 19:01 to 19:03 UTC, \`deploys.confirmed\` by \`target\` with a token of the owner, one ask at a time from one machine. Five asks a span, each sent to Cloudflare (\`until\` a minute earlier for each). The whole call is the caller's time, through the kernel and the core:

| span | \`cost.ms\` | the whole call | \`step\` | \`groups\` |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 15 minutes | 318 to 392 | 0.50 to 0.64 s | 15000 | 1 |
| 1 hour | 363 to 471 | 0.54 to 0.65 s | 60000 | 2 to 3 |
| 6 hours | 497 to 653 | 0.70 to 0.88 s | 360000 | 4 |
| 24 hours | 854 to 1095 | 1.04 to 1.35 s | 1440000 | 22 |
| 7 days | 5949 to 8302, and 1097 once | 6.18 to 8.56 s, and 1.30 s once | 10074000 to 10079000 | 7, and 1 once |

Each 7-day answer was made from a sample and was one query, as the service then sent (A query); the one of 1097 ms is the one that summed to 100. The last ask of each span was then asked five more times: 25 answers from the memory, the whole call 0.14 to 0.26 s. The deployer's lines \`at: "deploy.…"\` of those 7 days were 1466, 173 of them \`deploy.confirmed\`; the time over a Worker that writes more was not measured, and \`core.calls\` is not read by a token.

## Who can call

| Method | Rule |
|---|---|
| \`metric.query\` | \`${metricRules.query}\` |
| \`metric.list\` | \`${metricRules.list}\` |
| \`metric.put\` | \`${metricRules.put}\` |
| \`metric.delete\` | \`${metricRules.delete}\` |
| \`dashboard.list\` | \`${dashboardRules.list}\` |
| \`dashboard.get\` | \`${dashboardRules.get}\` |
| \`dashboard.put\` | \`${dashboardRules.put}\` |
| \`dashboard.delete\` | \`${dashboardRules.delete}\` |

So \`core.calls\` is read by the owner in their own tab, as \`logs.query\` is. A token of the owner reads \`deploys.*\`: counts of what \`logs.deploys\` already gives it. The rule reads \`metric\` from the query string, and a call with none is refused for every caller but the owner in their tab. The owner changes the rule with \`rule.put\` and no deploy.

\`metric.list\` does not follow the rule of \`metric.query\`: a token is listed \`core.calls\` and is refused it.

Whatever a rule has become, the service itself answers two kinds of caller and no other (\`metricTenant\`): the owner, with their tokens, and a member, a caller whose name starts \`did:\`. A Worker of the Brain (a caller named \`worker:…\`) and a stranger are answered 403 by every method. A member's Worker is not such a caller. The core sends its call on as its author's, and only for a method the owner granted that DID: the caller the service is given is the DID, with \`x-brain-via: worker:brain-m-ID-NAME\` (brain-core, \`asAuthor\`). So a member's Worker is answered as the member is: it writes, lists, reads and deletes its author's metrics and dashboards, and no other's.

## A member's metrics

A member's metric is named \`m.ID.NAME\` and is over a Worker \`brain-m-ID-SERVICE\`, where \`ID\` is the first ten hex digits of the SHA-256 of the member's DID (\`id\` of \`member.whoami\`; the same id as in the name of their Workers and their repositories). The service computes it from the caller on each call, and nothing a member sends changes it.

\`\`\`js
POST /xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.metric.put
{ "name": "m.0123456789.errors",          // m.ID. and then 1 to 30 of a-z, 0-9 and -
  "worker": "brain-m-0123456789-todo",    // brain-m-ID- and then the service's name, 1 to 20 of a-z and 0-9
  "at": "todo.error",                     // the \`at\` of the lines, 1 to 100 characters
  "value": null,                          // a field of the line that is a number, or null: the lines are counted
  "dims": [{ "key": "kind" }, { "key": "code", "type": "number" }] }   // 8 at most
\`\`\`

A field's name, in \`value\` and in a \`key\`, is a letter or \`_\` and then up to 63 letters, digits, \`_\` and \`.\`. A \`key\` is not \`metric\`, \`since\`, \`until\` or \`by\`, which are parameters of a query. A member keeps ${metricLimits.kept} metrics.

| A member's call | Answer |
|---|---|
| \`metric.put\` with a \`name\` that does not start \`m.ID.\` with their own id, or a \`worker\` that does not start \`brain-m-ID-\` with it | 403 |
| \`metric.put\` with their own name and Worker and a definition that is not one, or a new name when ${metricLimits.kept} are kept | 400 |
| \`metric.delete\` of a name that does not start \`m.ID.\` with their own id | 403 |
| \`metric.query\` of a metric that does not start \`m.ID.\` with their own id: another member's, and every metric of the Brain's own Workers | 403, the same for a name that is kept and one that is not |
| \`metric.query\` of their own name that is not kept | 404 |
| \`metric.list\` | their own definitions and no other |

The owner and their tokens are listed every definition, and are refused \`metric.put\` and \`metric.delete\` by the service (403): a metric written by the owner over a Worker of the Brain would give a token that Worker's lines under another name. The owner in their own tab reads a member's metric with \`metric.query\`, as they read every line with \`logs.query\`; a token does not, by the rule.

What holds one member's counts from another: the script Cloudflare is asked for is the \`worker\` of the definition, a definition is kept only with a \`worker\` of the member who put it, and it is read only by that member's own name. A kept row whose \`worker\` is not its member's (no method writes one) is answered 500 and Cloudflare is not asked.

**A member reaches these methods only when the owner granted them** (\`grant.put\` of each of the four for that DID): the kernel refuses a DID any method outside its own list before a rule is read.

**No price.** Each \`metric.query\` that is not answered from the memory is one query of Cloudflare's logs on the owner's account, or up to ${1 + metricPieceDefaults.most} for a span Cloudflare sampled (A query), and no method here has a price. What one such query costs was not found: Cloudflare prices Workers Logs by the lines written, and says a price for observability starts 2026-12-01 without giving it (read 2026-10-11, \`plan/cloud-brain-dashboard-service.md\`, "Read"). The core counts the calls a member's Worker makes against its author's calls for a day (2000 unless the owner set another; brain-core, \`asAuthor\`); a member's own call of a granted method was not found to be counted. A member's Worker is called by whoever its own rule lets in, so with the grant a caller of that Worker can make it send a \`metric.query\`, each a query on the owner's account, up to that count. What bounds a member's own calls today is the grant, which the owner takes back. The owner sets a price with no deploy: \`price.put { target: "com.lopecode.brain.metric.query", price: 'caller.kind == "did" ? 0.001 : 0.0' }\` would charge the account of a member's call a tenth of a cent a query (read in brain-core, \`priced\`, and not run; the number is an example, not a measure).

## Dashboards

A dashboard is a row of this service, added and changed with no deploy. It holds names only: no data, and no rule. The data of a panel is asked of \`metric.query\` by whoever draws it, and is answered or refused there for that caller, so a caller that reads a dashboard reads nothing of a metric by it. The service does not look whether a panel's \`metric\` is defined, or whether its \`by\` and \`filter\` name dimensions of it.

\`\`\`js
POST /xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.dashboard.put
{ "name": "deploys",                 // 1 to 30 of a-z, 0-9 and -; a member's is m-ID- and then that
  "title": "Deploys",                // 1 to 100 characters
  "panels": [                        // 1 to ${dashboardLimits.panels}
    { "title": "Confirmed, by Worker",          // 1 to 100 characters
      "metric": "deploys.confirmed",            // a metric's name: 1 to 80 of a-z, 0-9, . and -
      "by": ["target"],                         // dimensions to group by, 8 at most, each once; none when left out
      "filter": { "target": "brain-x-git" },    // a dimension and the value it has, 8 at most; none when left out
      "draw": "bars" }] }                       // one of ${dashboardDraws.join(", ")}
\`\`\`

The answer is the dashboard as kept: \`name\`, \`title\` and, for each panel, \`title\`, \`metric\`, \`by\`, \`filter\` and \`draw\`, with \`by\` a list and \`filter\` an object when they were left out. Any other field of the body or of a panel is not kept. A name in \`by\` and a key of \`filter\` is a field's name as a metric's dimension is, and a key is not \`metric\`, \`since\`, \`until\` or \`by\`; a value of \`filter\` is text of 200 characters at most, or a number. \`draw\` names how the page draws the panel: \`calls\`, \`faults\` and \`methods\` are for the rows of \`core.calls\`, \`bars\` and \`table\` for any metric. A body that is not this is answered 400 and nothing is kept.

The dashboards that are built in are a value of this module (\`dashboardDefinitions\`), as the Brain's own metrics are, and no method writes one: \`dashboard.put\` and \`dashboard.delete\` of a built-in name are answered 403 for every caller, and \`dashboard.get\` answers the module's value whatever row is kept under that name.

| Name | Title | Panel | Metric | By | Draw |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
${dashboardTable}

A member's dashboard is named \`m-ID-NAME\`, with the \`ID\` of their metrics. A caller keeps ${dashboardLimits.kept} dashboards: a member their own, and the owner with their tokens together the ones that are not a member's.

| Call | Answer |
|---|---|
| A member's \`dashboard.put\`, \`dashboard.get\` or \`dashboard.delete\` of a name that does not start \`m-ID-\` with their own id: another member's, the owner's, a built-in one | 403, the same for a name that is kept and one that is not |
| A member's \`dashboard.list\` | their own and no other |
| The owner's, or a token's, \`dashboard.list\` and \`dashboard.get\` | every dashboard: the built-in ones, their own and each member's |
| The owner's, or a token's, \`dashboard.put\` or \`dashboard.delete\` of a name that starts \`m-\` | 403: a member's dashboard is written by the member, and the owner keeps no name that starts \`m-\` |
| \`dashboard.put\` of a new name when ${dashboardLimits.kept} are kept | 400 |

The owner and a token of theirs are one caller to this service (the core sends both as \`owner\`), so a token that names \`dashboard.put\` writes the owner's dashboards. It does not write a member's, and it does not change \`health\`.

**A member reaches these methods only when the owner granted them**, as for the metrics: \`grant.put\` of each of the four for that DID.

## The Cloudflare token

The service declares \`cloudflare: ["Workers Observability Read"]\`, as brain-logs does. The deployer mints a token with that one permission and binds it to this Worker alone. It reads the logs of every Worker on the Cloudflare account, which is why a caller's text reaches Cloudflare only as the value of a filter on a dimension the definition names, and the script and \`at\` are the definition's.

## Not known

A member's call on a running Brain: every answer to a member above is from the tests of this module, with the caller's name given to the service as the core gives it. How the page draws a panel: no page reads a dashboard yet, and \`draw\`, \`by\` and \`filter\` are kept as given. The time of a query of \`core.calls\`, which holds many more lines than the deploys measured above (What a query costs). Which asks Cloudflare answers from a sample: it was seen over 4 and 7 days and not over 5 and 6 (A query), and what decides it was not found. Which of the two numbers \`sampled\` is read from an answer of a Brain carries: the tests give the service each alone and both, and what cb4 answered first is in \`tools/cloud-brain/records/metric-query-sampled-unsaid.md\`. A sample taken when a line is written (a Worker's own sampling rate of its logs), which asking again in parts does not undo: such an answer keeps its \`sampled\`. What Cloudflare answers for a span that starts before the 7 days it keeps. The shape of an answer with no \`by\`: the service reads a group with no \`groups\` as one row a step.`
// %%
// The metrics of the Brain's own Workers. A value of the seed: no method writes one (plan/cloud-brain-dashboard-service.md, "Two kinds").
metricDefinitions = [
  { name: "core.calls", worker: "brain-core", at: "call", value: "ms", dims: [{ key: "worker" }, { key: "method" }, { key: "status", type: "number" }] },
  { name: "deploys.confirmed", worker: "brain-deployer", at: "deploy.confirmed", value: null, dims: [{ key: "target" }] },
  { name: "deploys.put-back", worker: "brain-deployer", at: "deploy.put-back", value: null, dims: [{ key: "target" }] },
  { name: "deploys.failed", worker: "brain-deployer", at: "deploy.failed", value: null, dims: [{ key: "target" }] }
]
// %%
// The definitions as rows of the reference's table. A cell of its own: a prose cell with a template inside a hole
// is not read as prose at the emit, and the Worker then serves a reference without it.
metricTable = {
  const code = (text) => "`" + text + "`";
  return metricDefinitions.map((d) => `| ${code(d.name)} | ${code(d.worker)} | ${code(`at: "${d.at}"`)} | ${d.value ? code(d.value) + ", summed, and its max" : "none: counted"} | ${d.dims.map((x) => code(x.key) + (x.type === "number" ? " (a number)" : "")).join(", ")} |`).join("\n");
}
// %%
// The rules, read by the service's manifest and by the reference above.
metricRules = ({
  query: 'caller.session || (caller.id == "owner" && request.params.metric.startsWith("deploys.")) || (caller.kind == "did" && request.params.metric.startsWith("m."))',
  list: 'caller.session || caller.id == "owner" || caller.kind == "did"',
  put: 'caller.kind == "did"',
  delete: 'caller.kind == "did"'
})
// %%
metricLimits = ({ kept: 50 })
// %%
// The dashboards that are built in. A value of the seed, as the Brain's own metrics are: no method writes one.
// health is the three panels the page draws today from the core's calls (healthView of cloud-brain.ojs).
dashboardDefinitions = [
  { name: "health", title: "Health", panels: ["calls", "faults", "methods"].map((draw, i) => ({ title: ["Calls", "Health", "By method"][i], metric: "core.calls", by: ["worker", "method", "status"], filter: {}, draw })) }
]
// %%
// How a panel is drawn. calls, faults and methods need the rows of core.calls; bars and table draw any metric.
dashboardDraws = ["calls", "faults", "methods", "bars", "table"]
// %%
// The built-in dashboards as rows of the reference's table, a row a panel. A cell of its own, as metricTable is.
dashboardTable = {
  const code = (text) => "`" + text + "`";
  return dashboardDefinitions.flatMap((d) => d.panels.map((p) => `| ${code(d.name)} | ${d.title} | ${p.title} | ${code(p.metric)} | ${p.by.map(code).join(", ")} | ${code(p.draw)} |`)).join("\n");
}
// %%
dashboardRules = (({ all }) => ({ list: all, get: all, put: all, delete: all }))({ all: 'caller.id == "owner" || caller.kind == "did"' })
// %%
dashboardLimits = ({ kept: 50, panels: 20 })
// %%
// Whether a caller may write a dashboard of this name: null, or { status: 403, error }. `id` is metricTenant's: "" the owner.
// A member writes m-<their id>-…; the owner and their tokens write no built-in name and no name of a member's.
dashboardHold = (id, name) => {
  const text = typeof name === "string" ? name : "";
  if (id) return text.startsWith("m-" + id + "-") ? null : { status: 403, error: `a member's dashboard is named m-${id}-NAME` };
  if (dashboardDefinitions.some((d) => d.name === text)) return { status: 403, error: `${text} is built in: a value of the seed, which no method writes` };
  if (text.startsWith("m-")) return { status: 403, error: "a member's dashboard is written by the member, and the owner keeps no name that starts m-" };
  return null;
}
// %%
// The body of a dashboard.put as the dashboard that is kept: { def }, or { status, error }.
// 403 for a name that is not the caller's to write, 400 for a dashboard that is not one. Names only: no metric is looked up.
dashboardOwn = (id, body) => {
  const b = body && typeof body === "object" ? body : {};
  const held = dashboardHold(id, b.name);
  if (held) return held;
  const start = id ? "m-" + id + "-" : "", field = /^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.]{0,63}$/;
  const text = (x) => typeof x === "string" && x.length >= 1 && x.length <= 100;
  if (typeof b.name !== "string" || !/^[a-z0-9-]{1,30}$/.test(b.name.slice(start.length))) return { status: 400, error: `name is ${start ? start + " and then " : ""}1 to 30 of a-z, 0-9 and -` };
  if (!text(b.title)) return { status: 400, error: "title is 1 to 100 characters" };
  if (!Array.isArray(b.panels) || b.panels.length < 1 || b.panels.length > dashboardLimits.panels) return { status: 400, error: `panels is a list of 1 to ${dashboardLimits.panels}` };
  const panels = [];
  for (const [i, p] of b.panels.entries()) {
    const no = (error) => ({ status: 400, error: `panel ${i + 1}: ${error}` });
    if (!p || typeof p !== "object") return no("{ title, metric, by, filter, draw }");
    if (!text(p.title)) return no("title is 1 to 100 characters");
    if (typeof p.metric !== "string" || !/^[a-z0-9.-]{1,80}$/.test(p.metric)) return no("metric is a metric's name, 1 to 80 of a-z, 0-9, . and -");
    const by = p.by == null ? [] : p.by;
    if (!Array.isArray(by) || by.length > 8 || !by.every((k) => typeof k === "string" && field.test(k)) || new Set(by).size !== by.length) return no("by is 8 at most of a dimension's name, each once");
    const filter = p.filter == null ? {} : p.filter;
    const value = (v) => (typeof v === "string" && v.length <= 200) || (typeof v === "number" && Number.isFinite(v));
    if (typeof filter !== "object" || Array.isArray(filter) || Object.keys(filter).length > 8 || !Object.entries(filter).every(([k, v]) => field.test(k) && !["metric", "since", "until", "by"].includes(k) && value(v))) return no("filter is 8 at most of a dimension's name with its value, text of 200 characters at most or a number; a name is not metric, since, until or by");
    if (!dashboardDraws.includes(p.draw)) return no("draw is one of " + dashboardDraws.join(", "));
    panels.push({ title: p.title, metric: p.metric, by: [...by], filter: { ...filter }, draw: p.draw });
  }
  return { def: { name: b.name, title: b.title, panels } };
}
// %%
// Who a caller is to this service, whatever a rule passed: { id: "" } the owner and their tokens, { id } a member
// (the 10 hex of the SHA-256 of the DID that brain-deployer and brain-git name a member's things by), null anyone else.
metricTenant = async (caller) => (caller === "owner" ? { id: "" } : /^did:/.test(caller || "") ? { id: (await sha256(caller)).slice(0, 10) } : null)
// %%
// The body of a member's metric.put as the definition that is kept: { def }, or { status, error }.
// 403 for a name or a Worker that is not this member's, 400 for a definition that is not one.
metricOwn = (id, body) => {
  const b = body && typeof body === "object" ? body : {};
  const name = "m." + id + ".", worker = "brain-m-" + id + "-", field = /^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.]{0,63}$/;
  if (typeof b.name !== "string" || !b.name.startsWith(name)) return { status: 403, error: `a member's metric is named ${name}NAME` };
  if (typeof b.worker !== "string" || !b.worker.startsWith(worker)) return { status: 403, error: `a member's metric is over a Worker of their own, ${worker}SERVICE` };
  if (!/^[a-z0-9-]{1,30}$/.test(b.name.slice(name.length))) return { status: 400, error: `name is ${name} and then 1 to 30 of a-z, 0-9 and -` };
  if (!/^[a-z0-9]{1,20}$/.test(b.worker.slice(worker.length))) return { status: 400, error: `worker is ${worker} and then the service's name, 1 to 20 of a-z and 0-9` };
  if (typeof b.at !== "string" || b.at.length < 1 || b.at.length > 100) return { status: 400, error: "at is the `at` of the lines, 1 to 100 characters" };
  if (!(b.value == null || (typeof b.value === "string" && field.test(b.value)))) return { status: 400, error: "value is a field of the line that is a number, or null: the lines are counted" };
  const dims = b.dims == null ? [] : b.dims;
  const ok = (d) => d && typeof d === "object" && typeof d.key === "string" && field.test(d.key) && !["metric", "since", "until", "by"].includes(d.key) && (d.type == null || d.type === "string" || d.type === "number");
  if (!Array.isArray(dims) || dims.length > 8 || !dims.every(ok) || new Set(dims.map((d) => d.key)).size !== dims.length) return { status: 400, error: 'dims is 8 at most of { key } or { key, type: "number" }, each key once; a key is a field of the line and not metric, since, until or by' };
  return { def: { name: b.name, worker: b.worker, at: b.at, value: b.value == null ? null : b.value, dims: dims.map((d) => (d.type === "number" ? { key: d.key, type: "number" } : { key: d.key })) } };
}
// %%
// What a caller asked of one metric, from the query string: { since, until, by, where }, or { error } for a 400.
// A name in `by` or a filter that is not a dimension of the definition is an error, never dropped.
// since and until are cut to the minute they are in, so asks made within one minute are one query.
metricAsk = (def, params, now) => {
  const given = (name, or) => (params.has(name) ? (/^\d{1,15}$/.test(params.get(name)) ? Number(params.get(name)) : NaN) : or);
  const minute = (t) => Math.floor(t / 60000) * 60000;
  const until = minute(given("until", now)), since = minute(given("since", until - 3600000));
  if (!(since >= 0 && since < until)) return { error: "since and until are times in milliseconds, each cut to its minute: since is in a minute before until's" };
  const dims = new Map(def.dims.map((d) => [d.key, d.type || "string"]));
  const names = `the dimensions of ${def.name} are ${[...dims.keys()].join(", ")}`;
  const by = (params.get("by") || "").split(",").filter((k) => k !== "");
  if (by.some((k) => !dims.has(k)) || new Set(by).size !== by.length) return { error: "by is a list of dimensions, each once: " + names };
  const where = [];
  for (const [key, value] of params) {
    if (["metric", "since", "until", "by"].includes(key)) continue;
    if (!dims.has(key)) return { error: `${key} is not a parameter or a dimension: ` + names };
    const type = dims.get(key);
    if (type === "number" && !/^-?\d{1,15}$/.test(value)) return { error: `${key} is a whole number` };
    where.push({ key, operation: "eq", type, value: type === "number" ? Number(value) : value });
  }
  return { since, until, by, where };
}
// %%
// Cloudflare's telemetry query for one ask of one definition, inside the script of the definition's Worker.
metricBody = (def, ask, base) => {
  const dims = new Map(def.dims.map((d) => [d.key, d.type || "string"]));
  return logsScope({
    queryId: "metric " + def.name,
    timeframe: { from: ask.since, to: ask.until },
    view: "calculations",
    parameters: {
      calculations: [{ operator: "count" }, ...(def.value ? [{ operator: "sum", key: def.value, keyType: "number" }, { operator: "max", key: def.value, keyType: "number" }] : [])],
      groupBys: ask.by.map((key) => ({ type: dims.get(key), value: key })),
      filters: [{ key: "at", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: def.at }, ...ask.where],
      limit: 500
    }
  }, "query", base, def.worker);
}
// %%
// Cloudflare's `result` as rows { t, …the dimensions asked, n, sum, max }, one a step and group, oldest first.
// `sampled` is 1 for an answer made from every line, and more when Cloudflare says it counted from a sample: the most of
// run.statistics.abr_level and the sampleInterval of each row, either of which may be absent.
metricSeries = (result, def, by) => {
  const calcs = (result && result.calculations) || [];
  const of = (name) => calcs.find((c) => String(c.calculation).toLowerCase().startsWith(name)) || { series: [], aggregates: [] };
  const dims = new Map(def.dims.map((d) => [d.key, d.type || "string"]));
  const rows = new Map();
  const field = (name, key) => {
    for (const point of of(name).series || [])
      for (const g of point.data || []) {
        const t = Date.parse(String(point.time).replace(" ", "T") + "Z");
        const values = by.map((k) => ((g.groups || []).find((x) => x.key === k) || {}).value);
        const id = JSON.stringify([t, values]);
        if (!rows.has(id)) rows.set(id, { t, ...Object.fromEntries(by.map((k, i) => [k, dims.get(k) === "number" ? Number(values[i]) : String(values[i])])), n: 0, sum: def.value ? 0 : null, max: def.value ? 0 : null });
        rows.get(id)[key] = Number(g.value) || 0;
      }
  };
  field("count", "n");
  if (def.value) field("sum", "sum"), field("max", "max");
  const run = (result && result.run) || {}, most = (...xs) => Math.max(1, ...xs.map((x) => Number(x) || 1));
  const sampled = most((run.statistics || {}).abr_level, ...calcs.flatMap((c) => [...(c.aggregates || []), ...(c.series || []).flatMap((p) => p.data || [])]).map((g) => g && g.sampleInterval));
  return { step: run.granularity || 60000, groups: (of("count").aggregates || []).length, sampled, series: [...rows.values()].filter((r) => r.n > 0).sort((a, b) => a.t - b.t) };
}
// %%
// A sampled span is asked again in parts of `ms` (the setting pieceMs stands in for it; under a minute, no part is asked), when that is `most` parts or fewer.
metricPieceDefaults = ({ ms: 86400000, most: 8 })
// %%
// The parts of a span, oldest first, each `ms` long but the first, and each ending where the next starts: [[from, to], …].
// None for a span of `ms` or less, for more than `most` parts, and for an `ms` under a minute.
metricPieces = (since, until, ms = metricPieceDefaults.ms, most = metricPieceDefaults.most) => {
  if (!(ms >= 60000) || !(until - since > ms)) return [];
  const count = Math.ceil((until - since) / ms);
  return count > most ? [] : Array.from({ length: count }, (_, i) => [Math.max(since, until - (count - i) * ms), until - (count - i - 1) * ms]);
}
// %%
// The answers of the parts of one span (each a metricSeries) as one: the rows of all, a row of the same step and group in two
// parts added up. `step` is the longest of the parts' and `groups` the most any part answered; `sampled` is the highest.
metricJoin = (parts, by) => {
  const rows = new Map();
  for (const part of parts)
    for (const r of part.series) {
      const id = JSON.stringify([r.t, by.map((k) => r[k])]), had = rows.get(id);
      if (!had) rows.set(id, { ...r });
      else Object.assign(had, { n: had.n + r.n }, r.sum === null ? {} : { sum: had.sum + r.sum, max: Math.max(had.max, r.max) });
    }
  const top = (key) => Math.max(...parts.map((p) => p[key]));
  return { step: top("step"), groups: top("groups"), sampled: top("sampled"), series: [...rows.values()].sort((a, b) => a.t - b.t) };
}
// %%
// How long an answer of metric.query is kept (the setting memoryMs stands in for `ms`), and how much is kept at once.
metricMemoryDefaults = ({ ms: 60000, characters: 4000000 })
// %%
// A memory of answers of metric.query, as text, under the text of the query Cloudflare was sent.
// Text and never a promise: a promise made in one request is not awaited in another in a Worker.
// `now` and `ms` are the caller's, so a test moves the time. Oldest out first when `most` characters would be passed.
metricMemoryOf = (most = metricMemoryDefaults.characters) => {
  const kept = new Map();
  let held = 0;
  const drop = (key) => ((held -= key.length + kept.get(key).text.length), kept.delete(key));
  const fresh = (h, now, ms) => now >= h.at && now - h.at < ms;
  return {
    read: (key, now, ms) => (kept.has(key) && fresh(kept.get(key), now, ms) ? kept.get(key).text : null),
    keep: (key, text, now, ms) => {
      if (kept.has(key)) drop(key);
      for (const [k, h] of [...kept]) if (!fresh(h, now, ms)) drop(k);
      if (!(ms > 0) || key.length + text.length > most) return false;
      while (held + key.length + text.length > most) drop(kept.keys().next().value);
      kept.set(key, { at: now, text });
      held += key.length + text.length;
      return true;
    },
    held: () => ({ answers: kept.size, characters: held })
  };
}
// %%
// The memory of this instance of the Worker.
metricMemory = metricMemoryOf()
// %%
dashboard_service = cloudflare.Service(
  "dashboard",
  async (request, { caller }) => {
    const json = (status, body) => new Response(JSON.stringify(body), { status, headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
    const refuse = (status, error, message) => json(status, { error, message });
    const url = new URL(request.url), what = url.pathname.split("com.lopecode.brain.").pop();
    const verbs = { "metric.list": "GET", "metric.query": "GET", "metric.put": "POST", "metric.delete": "POST", "dashboard.list": "GET", "dashboard.get": "GET", "dashboard.put": "POST", "dashboard.delete": "POST" };
    if (!Object.hasOwn(verbs, what) || verbs[what] !== request.method) return refuse(404, "MethodNotImplemented", Object.entries(verbs).map(([name, verb]) => verb + " " + name).join(", "));
    // The tenant is held here, whatever a method's rule has become: a member reaches m.<their id>.… and m-<their id>-… and nothing else.
    const who = await metricTenant(caller);
    if (!who) return refuse(403, "Forbidden", "metrics and dashboards are for the owner and for a member");
    if (what.startsWith("dashboard.")) {
      const own = who.id ? "m-" + who.id + "-" : null;
      const builtIn = (name) => dashboardDefinitions.find((d) => d.name === name);
      // Every kept dashboard under a prefix. A row under a built-in name (no method writes one) is not read.
      const keptUnder = async (prefix) => (await rows.list("dashboard/" + prefix)).map((r) => r.value).filter((d) => !builtIn(d.name));
      // A member's count is their own; the owner's, with their tokens, the ones that are not a member's.
      const full = async () => (own ? await keptUnder(own) : (await keptUnder("")).filter((d) => !d.name.startsWith("m-"))).length >= dashboardLimits.kept;
      if (what === "dashboard.list") return json(200, { dashboards: (own ? await keptUnder(own) : [...dashboardDefinitions, ...(await keptUnder(""))]).map((d) => ({ name: d.name, title: d.title })) });
      if (what === "dashboard.get") {
        const name = url.searchParams.get("name") || "";
        if (own && !name.startsWith(own)) return refuse(403, "Forbidden", `a member reads their own dashboards, named ${own}NAME`);
        const found = builtIn(name) || (/^[a-z0-9-]{1,50}$/.test(name) ? await rows.get("dashboard/" + name) : null);
        return found ? json(200, { dashboard: found }) : refuse(404, "NotFound", `no dashboard ${name} is kept: dashboard.list names ${own ? "yours" : "them"}`);
      }
      const body = await request.json().catch(() => null);
      if (what === "dashboard.put") {
        const put = dashboardOwn(who.id, body);
        if (put.error) return refuse(put.status, put.status === 403 ? "Forbidden" : "InvalidRequest", put.error);
        if (!(await rows.get("dashboard/" + put.def.name)) && (await full())) return refuse(400, "InvalidRequest", `${dashboardLimits.kept} dashboards are kept: delete one first`);
        await rows.put("dashboard/" + put.def.name, put.def);
        return json(200, { dashboard: put.def });
      }
      const name = body && typeof body.name === "string" ? body.name : "";
      const held = dashboardHold(who.id, name);
      if (held) return refuse(held.status, "Forbidden", held.error);
      if (!/^[a-z0-9-]{1,50}$/.test(name) || !(await rows.get("dashboard/" + name))) return refuse(404, "NotFound", `no dashboard ${name} is kept`);
      await rows.delete("dashboard/" + name);
      return json(200, { deleted: name });
    }
    const mine = who.id ? "m." + who.id + "." : null;
    const kept = async (prefix) => (await rows.list("metric/" + prefix)).map((r) => r.value);
    if (what === "metric.list") return json(200, { metrics: mine ? await kept(mine) : [...metricDefinitions, ...(await kept("m."))] });
    if (what === "metric.put" || what === "metric.delete") {
      if (!mine) return refuse(403, "Forbidden", "a member writes their own metrics; a metric of the Brain's own Workers is a value of the seed");
      const body = await request.json().catch(() => null);
      if (what === "metric.put") {
        const own = metricOwn(who.id, body);
        if (own.error) return refuse(own.status, own.status === 403 ? "Forbidden" : "InvalidRequest", own.error);
        if (!(await rows.get("metric/" + own.def.name)) && (await kept(mine)).length >= metricLimits.kept) return refuse(400, "InvalidRequest", `a member keeps ${metricLimits.kept} metrics: delete one first`);
        await rows.put("metric/" + own.def.name, own.def);
        return json(200, { metric: own.def });
      }
      const name = body && typeof body.name === "string" ? body.name : "";
      if (!name.startsWith(mine)) return refuse(403, "Forbidden", `a member deletes their own metrics, named ${mine}NAME`);
      if (!(await rows.get("metric/" + name))) return refuse(404, "NotFound", `no metric ${name} is kept`);
      await rows.delete("metric/" + name);
      return json(200, { deleted: name });
    }
    const name = url.searchParams.get("metric") || "";
    if (mine && !name.startsWith(mine)) return refuse(403, "Forbidden", `a member reads their own metrics, named ${mine}NAME`);
    const def = metricDefinitions.find((d) => d.name === name) || (name.startsWith("m.") ? await rows.get("metric/" + name) : null);
    if (!def) return refuse(404, "NotFound", mine ? `no metric ${name} is kept: metric.list names yours` : "metric is one of " + metricDefinitions.map((d) => d.name).join(", ") + ", or a member's (metric.list)");
    // The script Cloudflare is asked for is the tenant: a kept definition is read only over a Worker of the member it is named for.
    if (!metricDefinitions.includes(def) && !String(def.worker).startsWith("brain-m-" + name.split(".")[1] + "-")) return refuse(500, "InternalError", `the kept definition of ${name} is not over a Worker of its member`);
    const ask = metricAsk(def, url.searchParams, Date.now());
    if (ask.error) return refuse(400, "InvalidRequest", ask.error);
    // The memory is read here, after every refusal above: a kept answer is given to no caller the service refuses.
    const body = JSON.stringify(metricBody(def, ask, config.base)), memoryMs = Number(config.memoryMs ?? metricMemoryDefaults.ms);
    const had = metricMemory.read(body, Date.now(), memoryMs);
    if (had) return json(200, { ...JSON.parse(had), cost: { ms: 0, queries: 0, cached: true } });
    const began = Date.now();
    // One query of Cloudflare: its answer as metricSeries, or { error } for a refusal.
    const send = async (text) => {
      const r = await cloudflareApi.fetch("/workers/observability/telemetry/query", { method: "POST", body: text });
      const data = await r.json().catch(() => null);
      return !r.ok || !data || !data.result ? { error: `Cloudflare answered ${r.status} ${JSON.stringify((data && data.errors) || null).slice(0, 300)}` } : metricSeries(data.result, def, ask.by);
    };
    let got = await send(body), queries = 1;
    // An answer made from a sample is asked again in parts, a day each, and the parts are the answer (metric-query-sampled-unsaid).
    const parts = got.error || got.sampled <= 1 ? [] : metricPieces(ask.since, ask.until, Number(config.pieceMs ?? metricPieceDefaults.ms));
    if (parts.length) {
      const answers = await Promise.all(parts.map(([from, to]) => send(JSON.stringify(metricBody(def, { ...ask, since: from, until: to }, config.base)))));
      queries += answers.length;
      got = answers.find((a) => a.error) || metricJoin(answers, ask.by);
    }
    if (got.error) return refuse(502, "UpstreamFailure", got.error);
    const ms = Date.now() - began, answer = { metric: def.name, since: ask.since, until: ask.until, ...got };
    metricMemory.keep(body, JSON.stringify(answer), Date.now(), memoryMs);
    return json(200, { ...answer, cost: { ms, queries, cached: false } });
  },
  {
    cloudflare: ["Workers Observability Read"],
    methods: {
      "com.lopecode.brain.metric.list": { type: "query", allow: metricRules.list },
      "com.lopecode.brain.metric.query": { type: "query", allow: metricRules.query },
      "com.lopecode.brain.metric.put": { type: "procedure", allow: metricRules.put },
      "com.lopecode.brain.metric.delete": { type: "procedure", allow: metricRules.delete },
      "com.lopecode.brain.dashboard.list": { type: "query", allow: dashboardRules.list },
      "com.lopecode.brain.dashboard.get": { type: "query", allow: dashboardRules.get },
      "com.lopecode.brain.dashboard.put": { type: "procedure", allow: dashboardRules.put },
      "com.lopecode.brain.dashboard.delete": { type: "procedure", allow: dashboardRules.delete }
    }
  }
)
// %%
dashboard_announce = {
  plugins.add("workers", dashboard_service, { invalidation });
  return "announced dashboard_service";
}
// %%
md`## Tests`
// %%
// The service with a stand-in for Cloudflare: `answer(body)` gives the result of one telemetry query, or a Response.
dashboardRig = async (answer = () => ({ run: { granularity: 60000 }, calculations: [] }), settings = {}) => {
  const seen = [];
  const sim = await simulate(dashboard_service, {
    secrets: { CF_TOKEN: "minted-1", BRAIN_KEY: "k" },
    config: { base: "cb4", account: "acct", ...settings },
    fetch: async (request) => {
      const body = await request.json();
      seen.push({ url: request.url, authorization: request.headers.get("authorization"), body });
      const out = answer(body);
      return out instanceof Response ? out : new Response(JSON.stringify({ success: true, result: out }), { headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
    }
  });
  // A token of the owner unless told: the owner with no tab.
  const token = { "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "delegation:b6559fa96c36", "x-brain-holder": "secret:loop-dashboard", "x-brain-tab": "0" };
  const call = async (method, query = "", { headers = token, verb = "GET", body = {} } = {}) => {
    const r = await sim.fetch("https://dashboard.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain." + method + query, { method: verb, headers, ...(verb === "GET" ? {} : { body: JSON.stringify(body) }) });
    return { status: r.status, data: await r.json() };
  };
  // A member: their id, and their calls. `write` is a POST with a body, `read` a GET.
  const member = async (did) => {
    const headers = { "x-brain-caller": did }, id = (await sha256(did)).slice(0, 10);
    return { did, id, write: (method, body) => call(method, "", { headers, verb: "POST", body }), read: (method, query = "") => call(method, query, { headers }) };
  };
  return { sim, seen, call, member };
}
// %%
// R1 of the spec: one body, written from the definition and from what was asked as data.
test_metric_query_sends_cloudflare_one_body_written_from_the_definition = {
  const H = 3600000, since = 1791676800000, until = since + H;
  // Cloudflare's shape as cb4 gave it on 2026-10-09 (test_calls_from_the_logs_become_chart_rows of the page): a list a calculation, a row a step and group.
  const group = (pairs, value) => ({ groups: Object.entries(pairs).map(([key, v]) => ({ key, value: v })), groupKey: Object.values(pairs).join(" ⬤ "), value });
  const calc = (calculation, aggregates, at) => ({ calculation, aggregates, series: Object.entries(at).map(([time, data]) => ({ time, data })) });
  const git = { target: "brain-x-git" }, echo = { target: "brain-x-echo" };
  const counted = { run: { granularity: 60000 }, calculations: [calc("count", [group(git, 3), group(echo, 1)], { "2026-10-11 16:01:00": [group(git, 2), group(echo, 1)], "2026-10-11 16:02:00": [group(git, 1)], "2026-10-11 16:03:00": [] })] };
  const rig = await dashboardRig((body) => (body.queryId === "metric core.calls" ? valued : counted));
  const out = await rig.call("metric.query", `?metric=deploys.confirmed&by=target&since=${since}&until=${until}`);
  expect(out.status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(1);
  expect(rig.seen[0]).toEqual({
    url: "https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/acct/workers/observability/telemetry/query",
    authorization: "Bearer minted-1",
    body: {
      queryId: "metric deploys.confirmed",
      timeframe: { from: since, to: until },
      view: "calculations",
      parameters: {
        datasets: ["cloudflare-workers"],
        filterCombination: "and",
        filters: [{ key: "$workers.scriptName", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: "cb4-deployer" }, { kind: "group", filterCombination: "and", filters: [{ key: "at", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: "deploy.confirmed" }] }],
        calculations: [{ operator: "count" }],
        groupBys: [{ type: "string", value: "target" }],
        limit: 500
      }
    }
  });
  const at = (minute) => Date.UTC(2026, 9, 11, 16, minute);
  const rest = ({ cost, ...data }) => data;
  expect(out.data.cost.cached).toBe(false);
  expect(rest(out.data)).toEqual({ metric: "deploys.confirmed", since, until, step: 60000, groups: 2, sampled: 1, series: [{ t: at(1), target: "brain-x-git", n: 2, sum: null, max: null }, { t: at(1), target: "brain-x-echo", n: 1, sum: null, max: null }, { t: at(2), target: "brain-x-git", n: 1, sum: null, max: null }] });
  // A metric with a value: its sum and max are asked, a number dimension is grouped and filtered as a number, and the script is the core's.
  const poll = { worker: "brain-x-inbox", status: 200 }, bad = { worker: "brain-x-inbox", status: 502 };
  const valued = { run: { granularity: 300000 }, calculations: [
    calc("count", [group(poll, 2), group(bad, 1)], { "2026-10-11 16:00:00": [group(poll, 2)], "2026-10-11 16:05:00": [group(bad, 1)] }),
    calc("sum(ms)", [], { "2026-10-11 16:00:00": [group(poll, 80)], "2026-10-11 16:05:00": [group(bad, 900)] }),
    calc("max(ms)", [], { "2026-10-11 16:00:00": [group(poll, 50)], "2026-10-11 16:05:00": [group(bad, 900)] })
  ] };
  const owner = { "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "session", "x-brain-tab": "1" };
  const calls = await rig.call("metric.query", `?metric=core.calls&by=worker,status&method=inbox.poll&status=200&since=${since}&until=${until}`, { headers: owner });
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(2);
  expect(rig.seen[1].body.parameters).toEqual({
    datasets: ["cloudflare-workers"],
    filterCombination: "and",
    filters: [{ key: "$workers.scriptName", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: "cb4-core" }, { kind: "group", filterCombination: "and", filters: [{ key: "at", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: "call" }, { key: "method", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: "inbox.poll" }, { key: "status", operation: "eq", type: "number", value: 200 }] }],
    calculations: [{ operator: "count" }, { operator: "sum", key: "ms", keyType: "number" }, { operator: "max", key: "ms", keyType: "number" }],
    groupBys: [{ type: "string", value: "worker" }, { type: "number", value: "status" }],
    limit: 500
  });
  expect(rest(calls.data)).toEqual({ metric: "core.calls", since, until, step: 300000, groups: 2, sampled: 1, series: [{ t: at(0), worker: "brain-x-inbox", status: 200, n: 2, sum: 80, max: 50 }, { t: at(5), worker: "brain-x-inbox", status: 502, n: 1, sum: 900, max: 900 }] });
  // With no span, the hour before now; with no `by`, no groupBys and one row a step.
  const whole = await dashboardRig(() => ({ run: { granularity: 60000 }, calculations: [calc("count", [{ value: 4 }], { "2026-10-11 16:01:00": [{ value: 4 }] })] }));
  const now = await whole.call("metric.query", "?metric=deploys.failed");
  expect(now.data.until - now.data.since).toBe(H);
  expect([now.data.until % 60000, now.data.since % 60000]).toEqual([0, 0]);
  expect(Math.abs(now.data.until - Date.now())).toBeLessThan(600000);
  expect(whole.seen[0].body.parameters.groupBys).toEqual([]);
  expect(now.data.series).toEqual([{ t: at(1), n: 4, sum: null, max: null }]);
  return "3 bodies";
}
// %%
// R3 of the spec: the rule on the method reads the metric's name.
test_metric_rules_give_a_token_the_deploy_counts_and_the_owners_tab_the_rest = {
  const { meta } = await dashboard_service.emit();
  // The five callers of brain-logs' rule test: the owner in a tab, a token of the owner, a member, a Worker, a stranger.
  const callers = [{ caller: "owner", via: "session", tab: true }, { caller: "owner", via: "delegation:b6559fa96c36", holder: "secret:loop-dashboard", tab: false }, { caller: "did:plc:member" }, { caller: "worker:brain-x-echo" }, { caller: "anonymous" }];
  const may = (nsid, params) => callers.map((who) => decide({ allow: meta.access[nsid].allow }, { caller: callerOf(who), origin: callerOf(who), request: { params } }).allow);
  const query = "com.lopecode.brain.metric.query", list = "com.lopecode.brain.metric.list", put = "com.lopecode.brain.metric.put", del = "com.lopecode.brain.metric.delete";
  const board = (name) => "com.lopecode.brain.dashboard." + name;
  expect(Object.entries(meta.access).map(([nsid, a]) => [nsid, a.type, a.allow])).toEqual([[board("delete"), "procedure", dashboardRules.delete], [board("get"), "query", dashboardRules.get], [board("list"), "query", dashboardRules.list], [board("put"), "procedure", dashboardRules.put], [del, "procedure", metricRules.delete], [list, "query", metricRules.list], [put, "procedure", metricRules.put], [query, "query", metricRules.query]]);
  // A dashboard: the owner in a tab, a token of the owner and a member. Which names each reaches is the service's.
  for (const name of ["list", "get", "put", "delete"]) expect([name, may(board(name), {}), meta.access[board(name)].price]).toEqual([name, [true, true, true, false, false], undefined]);
  expect(may(board("get"), { name: "health" })).toEqual([true, true, true, false, false]);
  // A write is a member's: not the owner in a tab, not a token.
  expect(may(put, {})).toEqual([false, false, true, false, false]);
  expect(may(del, {})).toEqual([false, false, true, false, false]);
  expect([meta.access[query].price, meta.access[put].price]).toEqual([undefined, undefined]);
  expect(may(query, { metric: "core.calls" })).toEqual([true, false, false, false, false]);
  expect(may(query, { metric: "deploys.confirmed" })).toEqual([true, true, false, false, false]);
  expect(may(query, { metric: "deploys.put-back" })).toEqual([true, true, false, false, false]);
  expect(may(query, { metric: "m.x.y" })).toEqual([true, false, true, false, false]);
  // A name that only holds "deploys." or "m." is not one that starts with it.
  expect(may(query, { metric: "core.deploys.x" })).toEqual([true, false, false, false, false]);
  expect(may(query, { metric: "xm.deploys." })).toEqual([true, false, false, false, false]);
  // With no metric the rule cannot be read: everyone but the owner in their tab is refused.
  expect(may(query, {})).toEqual([true, false, false, false, false]);
  expect(may(list, {})).toEqual([true, true, true, false, false]);
  return "15 rows of 5 callers";
}
// %%
// R3 of the spec: what the definition does not name is refused before Cloudflare is asked, and no method writes a definition.
test_metric_query_refuses_what_the_definition_does_not_name = {
  const since = 1791676800000, until = since + 3600000, span = `&since=${since}&until=${until}`;
  const rig = await dashboardRig();
  const owner = { headers: { "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "session", "x-brain-tab": "1" } };
  const status = async (method, query, options) => [query, (await rig.call(method, query, options)).status];
  // The core's line names who called. None of that is a dimension, in `by` or as a filter; nor is a dimension of another metric.
  for (const bad of ["&by=caller", "&by=worker,caller", "&by=holder", "&by=target", "&caller=owner", "&delegation=x", "&ray=a", "&by=worker,worker", "&status=2xx", "&status=200%20or%201", "&filters=x", "&worker=a&at=deploy.reason"])
    expect(await status("metric.query", "?metric=core.calls" + span + bad, owner)).toEqual(["?metric=core.calls" + span + bad, 400]);
  expect(await status("metric.query", "?metric=deploys.confirmed&by=worker" + span)).toEqual(["?metric=deploys.confirmed&by=worker" + span, 400]);
  // A span that is not one.
  // `until` alone under an hour would send Cloudflare a time before 1970 (a note of review 1502).
  for (const bad of [`&since=${until}&until=${since}`, `&since=${since}&until=${since}`, "&since=yesterday", `&since=${since}&until=`, "&since=-5", "&until=5", "&until=3599999"])
    expect(await status("metric.query", "?metric=deploys.confirmed" + bad)).toEqual(["?metric=deploys.confirmed" + bad, 400]);
  // A metric that is not defined, and no metric.
  for (const none of ["?metric=deploys.reason", "?metric=m.x.y", "?metric=", "", "?metric=core.calls%20"]) expect(await status("metric.query", none + (none ? span : ""), owner)).toEqual([none + (none ? span : ""), 404]);
  // No method writes a definition for the owner: a read is a GET, a write is a member's (403), and there is no other method.
  for (const [method, verb, status] of [["metric.put", "POST", 403], ["metric.delete", "POST", 403], ["metric.put", "GET", 404], ["metric.delete", "GET", 404], ["metric.query", "POST", 404], ["metric.list", "POST", 404], ["metric.define", "POST", 404], ["dashboard.put", "GET", 404], ["dashboard.get", "POST", 404], ["dashboard.query", "GET", 404], ["constructor", "GET", 404], ["logs.query", "POST", 404]])
    expect([method, verb, (await rig.call(method, "?metric=x.y", { ...owner, verb, body: { name: "core.mine", worker: "brain-core", at: "call", value: null, dims: [{ key: "caller" }] } })).status]).toEqual([method, verb, status]);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(0);
  expect((await rig.call("metric.list", "", owner)).data).toEqual({ metrics: metricDefinitions });
  expect(metricDefinitions.map((d) => d.name)).toEqual(["core.calls", "deploys.confirmed", "deploys.put-back", "deploys.failed"]);
  // A member with no metric of their own: no definition, and no data of any metric.
  const member = { headers: { "x-brain-caller": "did:plc:alicemember" } };
  expect(await rig.call("metric.list", "", member)).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { metrics: [] } });
  for (const name of ["deploys.confirmed", "core.calls", "m.x.y", ""]) expect(await status("metric.query", "?metric=" + name + span, member)).toEqual(["?metric=" + name + span, 403]);
  // Nothing above reached Cloudflare.
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(0);
  // Cloudflare's refusal is an error of this method, with its status named.
  const down = await dashboardRig(() => new Response('{"success":false,"errors":[{"code":10000,"message":"rate limited"}]}', { status: 429, headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } }));
  const out = await down.call("metric.query", "?metric=deploys.confirmed" + span);
  expect([out.status, out.data.error]).toEqual([502, "UpstreamFailure"]);
  expect(out.data.message).toContain("429");
  return "nothing sent to Cloudflare";
}
// %%
// R6 of the spec, the metric half: a member writes, lists, reads and deletes metrics over their own Workers, and no other's.
test_a_member_keeps_and_reads_metrics_of_their_own_workers_and_no_others = {
  const since = 1791676800000, until = since + 3600000, span = `&since=${since}&until=${until}`;
  const rig = await dashboardRig();
  const alice = await rig.member("did:plc:alice"), bob = await rig.member("did:plc:bob");
  const errors = (m, worker = "todo") => ({ name: `m.${m.id}.errors`, worker: `brain-m-${m.id}-${worker}`, at: "todo.error", value: null, dims: [{ key: "kind" }, { key: "code", type: "number" }] });
  // Over another member's Worker: refused, under either name. Over their own: kept, as the definition a built-in one is.
  expect((await alice.write("metric.put", { ...errors(alice), worker: `brain-m-${bob.id}-todo` })).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await alice.write("metric.put", { ...errors(bob), worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-todo` })).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await alice.write("metric.put", errors(bob))).status).toBe(403);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(0);
  expect(await alice.write("metric.put", errors(alice))).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { metric: errors(alice) } });
  expect((await alice.write("metric.put", { name: `m.${alice.id}.slow`, worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-todo`, at: "todo.done", value: "ms" })).data).toEqual({ metric: { name: `m.${alice.id}.slow`, worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-todo`, at: "todo.done", value: "ms", dims: [] } });
  expect((await bob.write("metric.put", errors(bob, "shop"))).status).toBe(200);
  expect([...rig.sim.rows.keys()].sort()).toEqual([`metric/m.${alice.id}.errors`, `metric/m.${alice.id}.slow`, `metric/m.${bob.id}.errors`].sort());
  expect(rig.sim.rows.get(`metric/m.${alice.id}.errors`)).toEqual(errors(alice));
  // The Brain's own Workers, a Worker that is not a member's, a name of the Brain's metrics: none is a member's to write.
  for (const body of [{ ...errors(alice), worker: "brain-core" }, { ...errors(alice), worker: "brain-x-git" }, { ...errors(alice), worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}` }, { ...errors(alice), name: "deploys.mine" }, { ...errors(alice), name: "core.calls" }, { ...errors(alice), name: `m.${alice.id}` }, { ...errors(alice), name: `m.${alice.id.toUpperCase()}.x` }, {}, null, "m"])
    expect([JSON.stringify(body), (await alice.write("metric.put", body)).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(body), 403]);
  // A definition that is not one: 400.
  const nine = Array.from({ length: 9 }, (_, i) => ({ key: "d" + i }));
  for (const change of [{ name: `m.${alice.id}.` }, { name: `m.${alice.id}.A` }, { name: `m.${alice.id}.a.b` }, { name: `m.${alice.id}.${"a".repeat(31)}` }, { worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-` }, { worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-to-do` }, { worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-${"a".repeat(21)}` }, { at: "" }, { at: 5 }, { at: "a".repeat(101) }, { value: 5 }, { value: "$workers.scriptName" }, { value: "a b" }, { dims: nine }, { dims: "kind" }, { dims: [{ key: "kind" }, { key: "kind" }] }, { dims: [{ key: "by" }] }, { dims: [{ key: "since" }] }, { dims: [{ key: "metric" }] }, { dims: [{ key: "$metadata.id" }] }, { dims: [{ key: "kind", type: "date" }] }, { dims: [null] }, { dims: ["kind"] }])
    expect([JSON.stringify(change).slice(0, 60), (await alice.write("metric.put", { ...errors(alice), ...change })).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(change).slice(0, 60), 400]);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(3);
  // The list: a member their own and no other, the owner and their tokens every definition.
  expect((await alice.read("metric.list")).data.metrics.map((d) => d.name)).toEqual([`m.${alice.id}.errors`, `m.${alice.id}.slow`]);
  expect((await bob.read("metric.list")).data).toEqual({ metrics: [errors(bob, "shop")] });
  expect((await rig.call("metric.list")).data.metrics.map((d) => d.name).sort()).toEqual([...metricDefinitions.map((d) => d.name), `m.${alice.id}.errors`, `m.${alice.id}.slow`, `m.${bob.id}.errors`].sort());
  // A read: their own is one body to Cloudflare inside the script of their own Worker. Another member's, and every built-in one, is 403.
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(0);
  const own = await alice.read("metric.query", `?metric=m.${alice.id}.errors&by=kind&code=500` + span);
  expect([own.status, own.data.metric, own.data.series]).toEqual([200, `m.${alice.id}.errors`, []]);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(1);
  expect(rig.seen[0].body.parameters).toEqual({
    datasets: ["cloudflare-workers"],
    filterCombination: "and",
    filters: [{ key: "$workers.scriptName", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: `cb4-m-${alice.id}-todo` }, { kind: "group", filterCombination: "and", filters: [{ key: "at", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: "todo.error" }, { key: "code", operation: "eq", type: "number", value: 500 }] }],
    calculations: [{ operator: "count" }],
    groupBys: [{ type: "string", value: "kind" }],
    limit: 500
  });
  for (const name of [`m.${bob.id}.errors`, `m.${bob.id}.none`, "deploys.confirmed", "deploys.put-back", "core.calls", "m.", "m", "", `M.${alice.id}.errors`, `xm.${alice.id}.errors`])
    expect([name, (await alice.read("metric.query", "?metric=" + name + span)).status]).toEqual([name, 403]);
  expect((await alice.read("metric.query", span.replace("&", "?"))).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await alice.read("metric.query", `?metric=m.${alice.id}.none` + span)).status).toBe(404);
  expect((await alice.read("metric.query", `?metric=m.${alice.id}.errors&by=caller` + span)).status).toBe(400);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(1);
  // The owner in their tab reads a member's metric by its name, as they read every line with logs.query.
  const tab = { headers: { "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "session", "x-brain-tab": "1" } };
  expect((await rig.call("metric.query", `?metric=m.${bob.id}.errors` + span, tab)).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.seen[1].body.parameters.filters[0].value).toBe(`cb4-m-${bob.id}-shop`);
  // A delete: their own. Another member's is 403 and stays.
  expect((await bob.write("metric.delete", { name: `m.${alice.id}.errors` })).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await alice.write("metric.delete", { name: "deploys.confirmed" })).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await alice.write("metric.delete", {})).status).toBe(403);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(3);
  expect(await alice.write("metric.delete", { name: `m.${alice.id}.errors` })).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { deleted: `m.${alice.id}.errors` } });
  expect((await alice.write("metric.delete", { name: `m.${alice.id}.errors` })).status).toBe(404);
  expect((await alice.read("metric.query", `?metric=m.${alice.id}.errors` + span)).status).toBe(404);
  expect([...rig.sim.rows.keys()].sort()).toEqual([`metric/m.${alice.id}.slow`, `metric/m.${bob.id}.errors`].sort());
  // Who is not a member writes nothing: the owner in their tab, a token, a caller named worker: (the core sends that name for a Worker of the Brain, never for a member's), a stranger, a DID spelled in capitals.
  const callers = [tab.headers, undefined, { "x-brain-caller": `worker:brain-m-${alice.id}-todo` }, { "x-brain-caller": "anonymous" }, {}, { "x-brain-caller": "DID:plc:alice" }, { "x-brain-caller": "deployer" }];
  for (const headers of callers) for (const method of ["metric.put", "metric.delete"])
    expect([JSON.stringify(headers), method, (await rig.call(method, "", { ...(headers ? { headers } : {}), verb: "POST", body: errors(alice) })).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(headers), method, 403]);
  // And who is neither the owner nor a member reads nothing, whatever the rule has become.
  for (const headers of callers.slice(2)) for (const [method, query] of [["metric.list", ""], ["metric.query", "?metric=deploys.confirmed" + span], ["metric.query", `?metric=m.${bob.id}.errors` + span]])
    expect([JSON.stringify(headers), method + query, (await rig.call(method, query, { headers })).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(headers), method + query, 403]);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(2);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(2);
  // A member's Worker, as the core sends its call on (asAuthor of brain-core): the caller is its author's DID, and via names the Worker.
  // It is answered as the member: alice's metrics, by any Worker of alice, and no other's.
  const todo = { "x-brain-caller": alice.did, "x-brain-via": `worker:brain-m-${alice.id}-todo`, "x-brain-tab": "0" };
  const asTodo = (method, query, body) => rig.call(method, query, { headers: todo, ...(body ? { verb: "POST", body } : {}) });
  expect((await asTodo("metric.put", "", errors(alice))).status).toBe(200);
  expect((await asTodo("metric.put", "", errors(alice, "other"))).status).toBe(200);
  expect((await asTodo("metric.list", "")).data.metrics.map((d) => d.name)).toEqual([`m.${alice.id}.errors`, `m.${alice.id}.slow`]);
  expect((await asTodo("metric.query", `?metric=m.${alice.id}.slow` + span)).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(3);
  expect(rig.seen[2].body.parameters.filters[0].value).toBe(`cb4-m-${alice.id}-todo`);
  for (const [method, query, body] of [["metric.put", "", errors(bob)], ["metric.put", "", { ...errors(alice), worker: `brain-m-${bob.id}-shop` }], ["metric.delete", "", { name: `m.${bob.id}.errors` }], ["metric.query", `?metric=m.${bob.id}.errors` + span], ["metric.query", "?metric=deploys.confirmed" + span], ["metric.query", "?metric=core.calls" + span]])
    expect([method + query, JSON.stringify(body || null).slice(0, 60), (await asTodo(method, query, body)).status]).toEqual([method + query, JSON.stringify(body || null).slice(0, 60), 403]);
  expect((await asTodo("metric.delete", "", { name: `m.${alice.id}.errors` })).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.get(`metric/m.${bob.id}.errors`)).toEqual(errors(bob, "shop"));
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(2);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(3);
  // 50 metrics a member: the 51st name is refused, a kept name is still written over.
  for (let i = 0; i < 49; i++) rig.sim.rows.set(`metric/m.${alice.id}.n${i}`, { ...errors(alice), name: `m.${alice.id}.n${i}` });
  expect((await alice.write("metric.put", { ...errors(alice), name: `m.${alice.id}.one-more` })).status).toBe(400);
  expect((await alice.write("metric.put", { ...errors(alice), name: `m.${alice.id}.slow`, at: "todo.slow" })).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.get(`metric/m.${alice.id}.slow`).at).toBe("todo.slow");
  expect((await bob.write("metric.put", { ...errors(bob), name: `m.${bob.id}.second` })).status).toBe(200);
  // A row that names a Worker which is not its member's (no method writes one) is not read from Cloudflare.
  rig.sim.rows.set(`metric/m.${alice.id}.n0`, { ...errors(alice), name: `m.${alice.id}.n0`, worker: "brain-core" });
  expect((await alice.read("metric.query", `?metric=m.${alice.id}.n0` + span)).status).toBe(500);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(3);
  return "3 bodies sent to Cloudflare";
}
// %%
// R4 and R8 of the spec: a dashboard is put, read, listed and deleted as a row, and health is a value of the module that no put or delete reaches.
test_a_dashboard_is_kept_as_data_and_health_is_built_in = {
  const rig = await dashboardRig();
  const tab = { headers: { "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "session", "x-brain-tab": "1" } };
  const post = (method, body, options = {}) => rig.call(method, "", { ...options, verb: "POST", body });
  // R8: with no row, health is three panels over core.calls, the three the page draws today.
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(0);
  const calls = (title, draw) => ({ title, metric: "core.calls", by: ["worker", "method", "status"], filter: {}, draw });
  const health = { name: "health", title: "Health", panels: [calls("Calls", "calls"), calls("Health", "faults"), calls("By method", "methods")] };
  expect(await rig.call("dashboard.get", "?name=health")).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { dashboard: health } });
  expect(await rig.call("dashboard.get", "?name=health", tab)).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { dashboard: health } });
  expect((await rig.call("dashboard.list")).data).toEqual({ dashboards: [{ name: "health", title: "Health" }] });
  expect(dashboardDefinitions.map((d) => d.name)).toEqual(["health"]);
  // Every panel of a built-in dashboard is over a metric of the module, by dimensions of it, drawn one of the five ways.
  for (const d of dashboardDefinitions) {
    expect(dashboardOwn("", { ...d, name: "copy" })).toEqual({ def: { ...d, name: "copy" } });
    for (const p of d.panels) expect([p.title, p.by.every((k) => metricDefinitions.find((m) => m.name === p.metric).dims.some((x) => x.key === k)), dashboardDraws.includes(p.draw)]).toEqual([p.title, true, true]);
  }
  // No put and no delete of the built-in name, by a token or by the owner in a tab: 403, and no row.
  const mine = { name: "health", title: "Mine", panels: [{ title: "One", metric: "deploys.failed", draw: "table" }] };
  for (const who of [{}, tab]) {
    expect([(await post("dashboard.put", mine, who)).status, (await post("dashboard.delete", { name: "health" }, who)).status]).toEqual([403, 403]);
    expect((await rig.call("dashboard.get", "?name=health", who)).data).toEqual({ dashboard: health });
  }
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(0);
  // A row under the built-in name (no method writes one) is not what is read or listed.
  rig.sim.rows.set("dashboard/health", mine);
  expect((await rig.call("dashboard.get", "?name=health")).data).toEqual({ dashboard: health });
  expect((await rig.call("dashboard.list")).data).toEqual({ dashboards: [{ name: "health", title: "Health" }] });
  rig.sim.rows.delete("dashboard/health");
  // R4: a second dashboard is a put. It is answered as kept, read back the same, and listed, by a token.
  const deploys = { name: "deploys", title: "Deploys", panels: [{ title: "Confirmed, by Worker", metric: "deploys.confirmed", by: ["target"], draw: "bars" }, { title: "Put back", metric: "deploys.put-back", by: ["target"], draw: "table" }] };
  const kept = { ...deploys, panels: deploys.panels.map((p) => ({ title: p.title, metric: p.metric, by: p.by, filter: {}, draw: p.draw })) };
  expect((await rig.call("dashboard.get", "?name=deploys")).status).toBe(404);
  expect(await post("dashboard.put", deploys)).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { dashboard: kept } });
  expect([...rig.sim.rows.entries()]).toEqual([["dashboard/deploys", kept]]);
  expect(await rig.call("dashboard.get", "?name=deploys")).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { dashboard: kept } });
  expect(await rig.call("dashboard.get", "?name=deploys", tab)).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { dashboard: kept } });
  expect((await rig.call("dashboard.list")).data).toEqual({ dashboards: [{ name: "health", title: "Health" }, { name: "deploys", title: "Deploys" }] });
  // A kept name is written over. What is not a field of a dashboard is not kept; by and filter are, as given.
  const one = { title: "One Worker", metric: "m.0123456789.errors", by: ["kind", "code"], filter: { target: "brain-x-git", status: 502 }, draw: "bars" };
  expect((await post("dashboard.put", { name: "deploys", title: "Deploys 2", panels: [{ ...one, rule: "true", data: [1] }], owner: "did:plc:x", rule: "true" }, tab)).data).toEqual({ dashboard: { name: "deploys", title: "Deploys 2", panels: [one] } });
  expect([...rig.sim.rows.entries()]).toEqual([["dashboard/deploys", { name: "deploys", title: "Deploys 2", panels: [one] }]]);
  // A dashboard holds names only: a metric that is not defined is kept, and nothing here asks Cloudflare.
  expect((await post("dashboard.put", { name: "later", title: "Later", panels: [{ title: "Not yet", metric: "flow.lead-time", draw: "table" }] })).status).toBe(200);
  // A dashboard that is not one: 400, and nothing is kept.
  const panel = deploys.panels[0], twentyOne = Array.from({ length: dashboardLimits.panels + 1 }, () => panel);
  const bad = [{ name: "" }, { name: "Deploys" }, { name: "a.b" }, { name: "a/b" }, { name: "a".repeat(31) }, { name: 5 }, { name: undefined }, { title: "" }, { title: 5 }, { title: "a".repeat(101) }, { panels: [] }, { panels: "x" }, { panels: undefined }, { panels: twentyOne }, { panels: [null] }, { panels: ["deploys.confirmed"] },
    ...[{ title: "" }, { title: undefined }, { metric: "" }, { metric: "Core.calls" }, { metric: "a b" }, { metric: 5 }, { metric: "a".repeat(81) }, { by: "target" }, { by: ["target", "target"] }, { by: ["$workers.scriptName"] }, { by: [5] }, { by: Array.from({ length: 9 }, (_, i) => "d" + i) }, { filter: "target" }, { filter: ["target"] }, { filter: { by: "x" } }, { filter: { since: 1 } }, { filter: { "a b": "x" } }, { filter: { target: null } }, { filter: { target: { a: 1 } } }, { filter: { target: "a".repeat(201) } }, { filter: Object.fromEntries(Array.from({ length: 9 }, (_, i) => ["d" + i, "x"])) }, { draw: "pie" }, { draw: undefined }, { draw: ["bars"] }].map((change) => ({ panels: [{ ...panel, ...change }] }))];
  for (const change of bad) expect([JSON.stringify(change).slice(0, 70), (await post("dashboard.put", { ...deploys, name: "wrong", ...change })).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(change).slice(0, 70), 400]);
  for (const body of [null, "deploys", [], {}]) expect([JSON.stringify(body), (await post("dashboard.put", body)).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(body), 400]);
  expect([...rig.sim.rows.keys()].sort()).toEqual(["dashboard/deploys", "dashboard/later"]);
  // A name that is not kept: 404 for a read and for a delete. A delete takes the row and no other.
  for (const none of ["?name=wrong", "?name=", "", "?name=metric/x", "?name=Deploys", "?name=deploys%20"]) expect([none, (await rig.call("dashboard.get", none)).status]).toEqual([none, 404]);
  for (const body of [{ name: "wrong" }, { name: "" }, {}, null, { name: "../metric/x" }, { name: 5 }]) expect([JSON.stringify(body), (await post("dashboard.delete", body)).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(body), 404]);
  expect(await post("dashboard.delete", { name: "later" })).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { deleted: "later" } });
  expect((await post("dashboard.delete", { name: "later" })).status).toBe(404);
  expect([...rig.sim.rows.keys()]).toEqual(["dashboard/deploys"]);
  // 50 dashboards for the owner and their tokens together: the 51st name is refused, a kept name is still written over. A member's are not counted.
  for (let i = 0; i < dashboardLimits.kept - 1; i++) rig.sim.rows.set("dashboard/n" + i, { ...kept, name: "n" + i });
  rig.sim.rows.set("dashboard/m-0123456789-theirs", { ...kept, name: "m-0123456789-theirs" });
  expect((await post("dashboard.put", { ...deploys, name: "one-more" })).status).toBe(400);
  expect((await post("dashboard.put", { ...deploys, name: "one-more" }, tab)).status).toBe(400);
  expect((await post("dashboard.put", { ...deploys, title: "Deploys 3" })).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.get("dashboard/deploys").title).toBe("Deploys 3");
  expect((await post("dashboard.delete", { name: "n0" })).status).toBe(200);
  expect((await post("dashboard.put", { ...deploys, name: "one-more" })).status).toBe(200);
  // A member's metric rows are not dashboards, and nothing above asked Cloudflare.
  expect((await rig.call("metric.list")).data).toEqual({ metrics: metricDefinitions });
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(0);
  return "health and " + dashboardLimits.kept + " kept";
}
// %%
// R6 of the spec, the dashboard half, and the two questions of review 1348 (N3): a member keeps dashboards named m-ID-NAME and reaches no other;
// the owner and their tokens read every one and write no member's.
test_a_member_keeps_dashboards_of_their_own_and_the_owner_writes_none_of_them = {
  const rig = await dashboardRig();
  const alice = await rig.member("did:plc:alice"), bob = await rig.member("did:plc:bob");
  const tab = { "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "session", "x-brain-tab": "1" };
  const board = (name, title = "Errors") => ({ name, title, panels: [{ title: "By kind", metric: "m." + name.split("-")[1] + ".errors", by: ["kind"], filter: {}, draw: "bars" }] });
  const hers = board(`m-${alice.id}-errors`), his = board(`m-${bob.id}-errors`, "Shop");
  // Kept as m-<id>-NAME, and under no other name: another member's, the owner's, a built-in one, their id with no name after it.
  expect(await alice.write("dashboard.put", hers)).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { dashboard: hers } });
  expect((await bob.write("dashboard.put", his)).status).toBe(200);
  expect([...rig.sim.rows.keys()].sort()).toEqual([`dashboard/m-${alice.id}-errors`, `dashboard/m-${bob.id}-errors`].sort());
  for (const name of [his.name, `m-${bob.id}-new`, "errors", "deploys", "health", `m-${alice.id}`, `m-${alice.id.toUpperCase()}-x`, `m.${alice.id}.errors`, `xm-${alice.id}-errors`, "", undefined, 5])
    expect([String(name), (await alice.write("dashboard.put", { ...hers, name })).status]).toEqual([String(name), 403]);
  for (const body of [null, "m", {}]) expect([JSON.stringify(body), (await alice.write("dashboard.put", body)).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(body), 403]);
  for (const change of [{ name: `m-${alice.id}-` }, { name: `m-${alice.id}-A` }, { name: `m-${alice.id}-a.b` }, { name: `m-${alice.id}-${"a".repeat(31)}` }, { title: "" }, { panels: [] }, { panels: [{ ...hers.panels[0], draw: "pie" }] }])
    expect([JSON.stringify(change).slice(0, 60), (await alice.write("dashboard.put", { ...hers, ...change })).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(change).slice(0, 60), 400]);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(2);
  // A read: their own. Another member's, the owner's and the built-in one are 403, the same for a name that is kept and one that is not.
  rig.sim.rows.set("dashboard/deploys", board("deploys", "Deploys"));
  expect(await alice.read("dashboard.get", "?name=" + hers.name)).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { dashboard: hers } });
  expect((await alice.read("dashboard.get", `?name=m-${alice.id}-none`)).status).toBe(404);
  for (const name of [his.name, `m-${bob.id}-none`, "deploys", "none", "health", "", `M-${alice.id}-errors`, `m-${alice.id}`])
    expect([name, (await alice.read("dashboard.get", "?name=" + name)).status]).toEqual([name, 403]);
  expect((await alice.read("dashboard.get", "")).status).toBe(403);
  // The list: a member their own and no other, not the built-in one.
  expect((await alice.read("dashboard.list")).data).toEqual({ dashboards: [{ name: hers.name, title: "Errors" }] });
  expect((await bob.read("dashboard.list")).data).toEqual({ dashboards: [{ name: his.name, title: "Shop" }] });
  // A delete: their own. Another member's, the owner's and the built-in one are 403 and stay.
  for (const name of [hers.name, "deploys", "health", `m-${alice.id}-none`, "", undefined]) expect([String(name), (await bob.write("dashboard.delete", { name })).status]).toEqual([String(name), 403]);
  expect((await bob.write("dashboard.delete", null)).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await alice.write("dashboard.delete", { name: `m-${alice.id}-none` })).status).toBe(404);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(3);
  // The owner in their tab and a token of the owner (one caller to the service): every dashboard is listed and read.
  for (const headers of [tab, undefined]) {
    const as = headers ? { headers } : {};
    expect((await rig.call("dashboard.list", "", as)).data.dashboards.map((d) => d.name).sort()).toEqual(["health", "deploys", hers.name, his.name].sort());
    expect((await rig.call("dashboard.get", "?name=" + hers.name, as)).data).toEqual({ dashboard: hers });
    // And no member's is written: not put over, not put new, not deleted. The token loop-dashboard names dashboard.* and is this caller.
    for (const [method, body] of [["dashboard.put", { ...hers, title: "Theirs" }], ["dashboard.put", board(`m-${alice.id}-new`)], ["dashboard.put", board("m-new")], ["dashboard.put", { ...hers, name: "m-" }], ["dashboard.delete", { name: hers.name }], ["dashboard.delete", { name: his.name }], ["dashboard.delete", { name: "m-none" }]])
      expect([method, body.name, (await rig.call(method, "", { ...as, verb: "POST", body })).status]).toEqual([method, body.name, 403]);
  }
  expect(rig.sim.rows.get("dashboard/" + hers.name)).toEqual(hers);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(3);
  // A member's Worker, as the core sends its call on (asAuthor and forward of brain-core): the caller is its author's DID and via names the Worker.
  // It is answered as the member: alice's dashboards and no other's.
  const todo = { "x-brain-caller": alice.did, "x-brain-via": `worker:brain-m-${alice.id}-todo`, "x-brain-tab": "0" };
  const asTodo = (method, query, body) => rig.call(method, query, { headers: todo, ...(body ? { verb: "POST", body } : {}) });
  expect((await asTodo("dashboard.put", "", board(`m-${alice.id}-second`, "Second"))).status).toBe(200);
  expect((await asTodo("dashboard.list", "")).data.dashboards.map((d) => d.name)).toEqual([hers.name, `m-${alice.id}-second`]);
  expect((await asTodo("dashboard.get", "?name=" + hers.name)).data).toEqual({ dashboard: hers });
  for (const [method, query, body] of [["dashboard.put", "", his], ["dashboard.put", "", board("deploys")], ["dashboard.delete", "", { name: his.name }], ["dashboard.delete", "", { name: "deploys" }], ["dashboard.get", "?name=" + his.name], ["dashboard.get", "?name=deploys"], ["dashboard.get", "?name=health"]])
    expect([method + query, body ? body.name : null, (await asTodo(method, query, body)).status]).toEqual([method + query, body ? body.name : null, 403]);
  expect((await asTodo("dashboard.delete", "", { name: `m-${alice.id}-second` })).status).toBe(200);
  // Who is neither the owner nor a member reaches no dashboard, whatever the rule has become: a Worker of the Brain, a stranger, no caller, a DID in capitals, the deployer.
  for (const headers of [{ "x-brain-caller": `worker:brain-m-${alice.id}-todo` }, { "x-brain-caller": "worker:brain-x-page" }, { "x-brain-caller": "anonymous" }, {}, { "x-brain-caller": "DID:plc:alice" }, { "x-brain-caller": "deployer" }])
    for (const [method, query, body] of [["dashboard.list", ""], ["dashboard.get", "?name=health"], ["dashboard.get", "?name=" + hers.name], ["dashboard.put", "", hers], ["dashboard.put", "", board("theirs")], ["dashboard.delete", "", { name: hers.name }]])
      expect([JSON.stringify(headers), method + query, (await rig.call(method, query, { headers, ...(body ? { verb: "POST", body } : {}) })).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(headers), method + query, 403]);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(3);
  // 50 a member: the 51st name is refused, a kept name is still written over, and the other member's count is their own.
  for (let i = 0; i < dashboardLimits.kept - 1; i++) rig.sim.rows.set(`dashboard/m-${alice.id}-n${i}`, board(`m-${alice.id}-n${i}`));
  expect((await alice.write("dashboard.put", board(`m-${alice.id}-one-more`))).status).toBe(400);
  expect((await alice.write("dashboard.put", { ...hers, title: "Errors 2" })).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.get("dashboard/" + hers.name).title).toBe("Errors 2");
  expect((await bob.write("dashboard.put", board(`m-${bob.id}-second`))).status).toBe(200);
  expect((await rig.call("dashboard.put", "", { verb: "POST", body: board("owners") })).status).toBe(200);
  // The delete is the member's own, and takes the one row.
  expect(await alice.write("dashboard.delete", { name: hers.name })).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { deleted: hers.name } });
  expect((await alice.read("dashboard.get", "?name=" + hers.name)).status).toBe(404);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.has("dashboard/" + his.name)).toBe(true);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(0);
  return "2 members, the owner and a token";
}
// %%
// R7 of the spec: a query asked again within the memory sends Cloudflare nothing, and the answer says which it was.
test_metric_query_asked_again_within_the_memory_sends_cloudflare_one_body = {
  const M = 60000, since = 1791676800000, until = since + 60 * M;
  const group = (target, value) => ({ groups: [{ key: "target", value: target }], groupKey: target, value });
  const counted = { run: { granularity: M }, calculations: [{ calculation: "count", aggregates: [group("brain-x-git", 3)], series: [{ time: "2026-10-11 16:01:00", data: [group("brain-x-git", 3)] }] }] };
  const rig = await dashboardRig(() => counted);
  const ask = (query, options) => rig.call("metric.query", "?metric=" + query, options);
  const q = `deploys.confirmed&by=target&since=${since}&until=${until}`;
  const first = await ask(q), second = await ask(q);
  expect([first.status, second.status, rig.seen.length]).toEqual([200, 200, 1]);
  expect([first.data.cost.queries, first.data.cost.cached, Number.isInteger(first.data.cost.ms) && first.data.cost.ms >= 0]).toEqual([1, false, true]);
  expect(second.data.cost).toEqual({ ms: 0, queries: 0, cached: true });
  const rest = ({ cost, ...data }) => data;
  expect(rest(second.data)).toEqual(rest(first.data));
  expect(rest(first.data)).toEqual({ metric: "deploys.confirmed", since, until, step: M, groups: 1, sampled: 1, series: [{ t: Date.UTC(2026, 9, 11, 16, 1), target: "brain-x-git", n: 3, sum: null, max: null }] });
  // The minutes: a since and an until anywhere inside the same two minutes are the same query, answered with the minutes.
  const inside = await ask(`deploys.confirmed&by=target&since=${since + 1}&until=${until + M - 1}`);
  expect([inside.data.since, inside.data.until, inside.data.cost.cached, rig.seen.length]).toEqual([since, until, true, 1]);
  // The owner in their tab asks the same query and is answered from the same memory: who asks is not part of the query.
  const tab = { headers: { "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "session", "x-brain-tab": "1" } };
  expect([(await ask(q, tab)).data.cost.cached, rig.seen.length]).toEqual([true, 1]);
  // Another minute, another by, a filter, another metric: each is another query, one body each, and each is then kept.
  const others = [`deploys.confirmed&by=target&since=${since}&until=${until + M}`, `deploys.confirmed&by=target&since=${since - M}&until=${until}`, `deploys.confirmed&since=${since}&until=${until}`, `deploys.confirmed&by=target&target=brain-x-git&since=${since}&until=${until}`, `deploys.failed&by=target&since=${since}&until=${until}`];
  for (const [i, other] of others.entries()) expect([other, (await ask(other)).data.cost.cached, rig.seen.length]).toEqual([other, false, 2 + i]);
  expect(rig.seen[1].body.timeframe).toEqual({ from: since, to: until + M });
  for (const other of [q, ...others]) expect([other, (await ask(other)).data.cost, rig.seen.length]).toEqual([other, { ms: 0, queries: 0, cached: true }, 6]);
  // A refusal is decided before the memory is read: a kept answer is given to nobody the service refuses.
  for (const headers of [{ "x-brain-caller": "did:plc:alice" }, { "x-brain-caller": "worker:brain-x-page" }, { "x-brain-caller": "anonymous" }, {}])
    expect([JSON.stringify(headers), (await ask(q, { headers })).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(headers), 403]);
  expect((await ask(`deploys.confirmed&by=caller&since=${since}&until=${until}`)).status).toBe(400);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(6);
  // A span that is one minute after the cut is not a span.
  expect((await ask(`deploys.confirmed&since=${since + 1}&until=${since + M - 1}`)).status).toBe(400);
  // Cloudflare's refusal is not kept: the next ask is sent.
  let down = true;
  const flaky = await dashboardRig(() => (down ? new Response('{"success":false,"errors":[{"code":10000,"message":"rate limited"}]}', { status: 429, headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } }) : counted));
  expect((await flaky.call("metric.query", "?metric=" + q)).status).toBe(502);
  down = false;
  expect([(await flaky.call("metric.query", "?metric=" + q)).data.cost.cached, (await flaky.call("metric.query", "?metric=" + q)).data.cost.cached, flaky.seen.length]).toEqual([false, true, 2]);
  // Another instance of the Worker has a memory of its own: the first ask there is sent.
  const other = await dashboardRig(() => counted);
  expect([(await other.call("metric.query", "?metric=" + q)).data.cost.cached, other.seen.length, rig.seen.length]).toEqual([false, 1, 6]);
  // The setting memoryMs is how long an answer is kept; 0 keeps none.
  const none = await dashboardRig(() => counted, { memoryMs: 0 });
  expect([(await none.call("metric.query", "?metric=" + q)).data.cost.cached, (await none.call("metric.query", "?metric=" + q)).data.cost.cached, none.seen.length]).toEqual([false, false, 2]);
  // A member's metric is kept under the query Cloudflare was sent: put again with another `at`, it is another query; deleted, it is 404.
  const alice = await rig.member("did:plc:alice"), bob = await rig.member("did:plc:bob");
  const errors = { name: `m.${alice.id}.errors`, worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-todo`, at: "todo.error", value: null, dims: [] };
  const mine = `?metric=m.${alice.id}.errors&since=${since}&until=${until}`;
  expect((await alice.write("metric.put", errors)).status).toBe(200);
  expect([(await alice.read("metric.query", mine)).data.cost.cached, (await alice.read("metric.query", mine)).data.cost.cached, rig.seen.length]).toEqual([false, true, 7]);
  expect((await bob.read("metric.query", mine)).status).toBe(403);
  // Each change of what Cloudflare is asked is another body; a dimension the query does not name is not, and the kept answer stands.
  const changes = [[{ at: "todo.failed" }, false], [{ at: "todo.failed", worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-shop` }, false], [{ at: "todo.failed", worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-shop`, value: "ms" }, false], [{ at: "todo.failed", worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-shop`, value: "ms", dims: [{ key: "kind" }] }, true]];
  let bodies = 7;
  for (const [change, cached] of changes) {
    expect((await alice.write("metric.put", { ...errors, ...change })).status).toBe(200);
    expect([JSON.stringify(change), (await alice.read("metric.query", mine)).data.cost.cached, rig.seen.length]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(change), cached, (bodies += cached ? 0 : 1)]);
  }
  // The type of a dimension the query names is part of what Cloudflare is asked.
  const last = { ...errors, ...changes[3][0] };
  expect([(await alice.read("metric.query", mine + "&by=kind")).data.cost.cached, rig.seen.length]).toEqual([false, 11]);
  expect((await alice.write("metric.put", { ...last, dims: [{ key: "kind", type: "number" }] })).status).toBe(200);
  expect([(await alice.read("metric.query", mine + "&by=kind")).data.cost.cached, rig.seen.length]).toEqual([false, 12]);
  expect((await alice.write("metric.delete", { name: errors.name })).status).toBe(200);
  expect([(await alice.read("metric.query", mine)).status, rig.seen.length]).toEqual([404, 12]);
  return "12 bodies";
}
// %%
// A stand-in for Cloudflare that samples: a timeframe longer than `whole` ms is answered from every tenth line, each
// counted as ten. `says` is how the answer tells it: "level" (run.statistics.abr_level), "interval" (sampleInterval of a row) or "both".
// A line is in a timeframe from its `from` and before its `to`; whether Cloudflare's is so was not read.
sampledAnswer = (lines, { whole, says = "both" }) => (body) => {
  const { from, to } = body.timeframe, step = (to - from) / 60, k = to - from > whole ? 10 : 1;
  const inside = lines.filter((l) => l.t >= from && l.t < to).filter((l, i) => i % k === 0);
  const row = (target, n) => ({ groups: [{ key: "target", value: target }], groupKey: target, value: n * k, ...(says === "level" ? {} : { sampleInterval: k }) });
  const tally = (list) => [...list.reduce((m, l) => m.set(l.target, (m.get(l.target) || 0) + 1), new Map())].map(([target, n]) => row(target, n));
  const steps = new Map();
  for (const l of inside) { const t = from + Math.floor((l.t - from) / step) * step; steps.set(t, [...(steps.get(t) || []), l]); }
  const time = (t) => new Date(t).toISOString().slice(0, 19).replace("T", " ");
  return { run: { granularity: step, ...(says === "interval" ? {} : { statistics: { abr_level: k } }) }, calculations: [{ calculation: "count", aggregates: tally(inside), series: [...steps].map(([t, list]) => ({ time: time(t), data: tally(list) })) }] };
}
// %%
// metric-query-sampled-unsaid: an answer says whether Cloudflare made it from a sample, and a sampled span of days is asked again a day at a time.
test_metric_query_says_a_sample_and_asks_a_sampled_span_of_days_a_day_at_a_time = {
  const M = 60000, D = 86400000, until = 1791744660000, since = until - 7 * D;
  // 173 lines over the last four of seven days, as cb4 had on 2026-10-11; three targets, the third with one line in nine.
  const lines = Array.from({ length: 173 }, (_, i) => ({ t: since + 3 * D + Math.floor((i * 4 * D) / 173), target: i % 9 === 4 ? "brain-db" : i % 2 ? "brain" : "brain-core" }));
  const byTarget = (list, n = () => 1) => Object.fromEntries([...list.reduce((m, l) => m.set(l.target, (m.get(l.target) || 0) + n(l)), new Map())].sort());
  const span = (a, b) => `?metric=deploys.confirmed&by=target&since=${a}&until=${b}`;
  const frames = (rig, from = 0) => rig.seen.slice(from).map((s) => [s.body.timeframe.from, s.body.timeframe.to]);
  const days = Array.from({ length: 7 }, (_, i) => [since + i * D, since + (i + 1) * D]);
  // Sampled over three days, as cb4 was seen to be over four and seven: the span is asked, and then each of its days.
  const rig = await dashboardRig(sampledAnswer(lines, { whole: 3 * D }));
  const week = await rig.call("metric.query", span(since, until));
  expect([week.status, week.data.sampled, rig.seen.length]).toEqual([200, 1, 8]);
  expect(frames(rig)).toEqual([[since, until], ...days]);
  expect([week.data.cost.queries, week.data.cost.cached, week.data.step, week.data.groups]).toEqual([8, false, D / 60, 3]);
  expect(byTarget(week.data.series, (r) => r.n)).toEqual(byTarget(lines));
  expect(week.data.series.map((r) => r.t)).toEqual([...week.data.series.map((r) => r.t)].sort((a, b) => a - b));
  // The parts are sent as the span is but for the timeframe.
  for (const s of rig.seen.slice(1)) expect({ ...s.body, timeframe: null }).toEqual({ ...rig.seen[0].body, timeframe: null });
  // Asked again, the joined answer is the one kept: nothing is sent.
  const again = await rig.call("metric.query", span(since, until));
  expect([again.data.cost, again.data.sampled, rig.seen.length]).toEqual([{ ms: 0, queries: 0, cached: true }, 1, 8]);
  expect(again.data.series).toEqual(week.data.series);
  // A span that Cloudflare answers whole is one body, whatever its length.
  for (const [a, n] of [[until - 60 * M, 9], [until - 3 * D, 10]]) expect([(await rig.call("metric.query", span(a, until))).data.sampled, rig.seen.length]).toEqual([1, n]);
  // A span that is not whole days: the first part is the short one, and `step` is the longest of the parts'.
  const odd = await rig.call("metric.query", span(since + 2 * D - 30 * M, until));
  expect([odd.data.sampled, odd.data.cost.queries, odd.data.step]).toEqual([1, 7, D / 60]);
  expect(frames(rig, 10)).toEqual([[since + 2 * D - 30 * M, until], [since + 2 * D - 30 * M, since + 2 * D], ...days.slice(2)]);
  expect(byTarget(odd.data.series, (r) => r.n)).toEqual(byTarget(lines));
  // What a sample is, with nothing asked again: every n a multiple of 10, and a target left out. The answer says 10.
  const off = await dashboardRig(sampledAnswer(lines, { whole: 3 * D }), { pieceMs: 0 });
  const short = await off.call("metric.query", span(since, until));
  expect([short.data.sampled, short.data.cost.queries, off.seen.length, short.data.series.every((r) => r.n % 10 === 0)]).toEqual([10, 1, 1, true]);
  expect(byTarget(short.data.series, (r) => r.n)).not.toEqual(byTarget(lines));
  // Cloudflare tells it in two places, and either alone is read.
  for (const says of ["level", "interval"]) {
    const one = await dashboardRig(sampledAnswer(lines, { whole: 3 * D, says }), { pieceMs: 0 });
    expect([says, (await one.call("metric.query", span(since, until))).data.sampled, (await one.call("metric.query", span(until - D, until))).data.sampled]).toEqual([says, 10, 1]);
    const parts = await dashboardRig(sampledAnswer(lines, { whole: 3 * D, says }));
    expect([says, (await parts.call("metric.query", span(since, until))).data.sampled, parts.seen.length]).toEqual([says, 1, 8]);
  }
  // A day that is itself sampled: the parts are answered, and the answer says 10. A span of a day or less is asked once.
  const all = await dashboardRig(sampledAnswer(lines, { whole: 0 }));
  const still = await all.call("metric.query", span(since, until));
  expect([still.status, still.data.sampled, still.data.cost.queries, all.seen.length]).toEqual([200, 10, 8, 8]);
  for (const [a, n] of [[until - D, 9], [until - 12 * 60 * M, 10], [until - D - M, 13]]) expect([a - until, (await all.call("metric.query", span(a, until))).data.sampled, all.seen.length]).toEqual([a - until, 10, n]);
  // More than 8 parts are not asked: the one answer, which says 10.
  const long = await all.call("metric.query", span(until - 8 * D - M, until));
  expect([long.data.sampled, long.data.cost.queries, all.seen.length]).toEqual([10, 1, 14]);
  expect([(await all.call("metric.query", span(until - 8 * D, until))).data.cost.queries, all.seen.length]).toEqual([9, 23]);
  // Cloudflare's refusal of one part is the answer's, and nothing is kept: the next ask sends all of it again.
  let sent = 0, down = true;
  const inner = sampledAnswer(lines, { whole: 3 * D });
  const flaky = await dashboardRig((body) => (++sent === 3 && down ? new Response('{"success":false,"errors":[{"code":10000,"message":"rate limited"}]}', { status: 429, headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } }) : inner(body)));
  expect([(await flaky.call("metric.query", span(since, until))).status, flaky.seen.length]).toEqual([502, 8]);
  down = false;
  const after = await flaky.call("metric.query", span(since, until));
  expect([after.status, after.data.sampled, after.data.cost.cached, flaky.seen.length]).toEqual([200, 1, false, 16]);
  return "173 lines";
}
// %%
// The parts of a span and the join of their answers, with no service.
test_metric_parts_abut_and_their_rows_are_joined = {
  const M = 60000, D = 86400000, T = 1791676800000;
  expect(metricPieceDefaults).toEqual({ ms: D, most: 8 });
  const parts = (...given) => metricPieces(...given).map(([a, b]) => [a - T, b - T]);
  // A day or less is no part; over it, days counted back from the end, the first the short one.
  expect([parts(T, T + D), parts(T, T + M), parts(T, T), parts(T + D, T)]).toEqual([[], [], [], []]);
  expect(parts(T, T + D + M)).toEqual([[0, M], [M, D + M]]);
  expect(parts(T, T + 3 * D)).toEqual([[0, D], [D, 2 * D], [2 * D, 3 * D]]);
  expect([parts(T, T + 8 * D).length, parts(T, T + 8 * D + M), parts(0, T)]).toEqual([8, [], []]);
  // Another length and another count; a length under a minute, or none, is no part.
  expect(parts(T, T + 150 * M, 60 * M)).toEqual([[0, 30 * M], [30 * M, 90 * M], [90 * M, 150 * M]]);
  expect([parts(T, T + 150 * M, 60 * M, 2), parts(T, T + 150 * M, 60 * M, 3).length]).toEqual([[], 3]);
  for (const ms of [0, -1, NaN, 59999]) expect([String(ms), parts(T, T + 3 * D, ms)]).toEqual([String(ms), []]);
  // Every part ends where the next starts, and the first and last are the span's ends.
  const week = metricPieces(T + 7 * M, T + 6 * D + 3 * M);
  expect([week[0][0], week.at(-1)[1], week.every(([a, b], i) => a < b && (i === 0 || a === week[i - 1][1]))]).toEqual([T + 7 * M, T + 6 * D + 3 * M, true]);
  // The join: rows of all parts by time, a row of one step and group in two parts added up, and the max the higher.
  const row = (t, worker, n, sum = null, max = null) => ({ t, worker, n, sum, max });
  const a = { step: 1000, groups: 2, sampled: 1, series: [row(1, "x", 2, 20, 15), row(5, "y", 1, 7, 7)] }, b = { step: 3000, groups: 1, sampled: 10, series: [row(5, "y", 3, 9, 4), row(5, "x", 1, 1, 1), row(9, "x", 4, 8, 8)] };
  expect(metricJoin([a, b], ["worker"])).toEqual({ step: 3000, groups: 2, sampled: 10, series: [row(1, "x", 2, 20, 15), row(5, "y", 4, 16, 7), row(5, "x", 1, 1, 1), row(9, "x", 4, 8, 8)] });
  expect(a.series[1]).toEqual(row(5, "y", 1, 7, 7));
  // A counted metric has no sum; with no `by`, one row a step.
  expect(metricJoin([{ step: 1, groups: 1, sampled: 1, series: [{ t: 1, n: 2, sum: null, max: null }] }, { step: 1, groups: 1, sampled: 1, series: [{ t: 1, n: 3, sum: null, max: null }] }], [])).toEqual({ step: 1, groups: 1, sampled: 1, series: [{ t: 1, n: 5, sum: null, max: null }] });
  // What Cloudflare says of a sample, in an answer: the level, a row's interval in the totals or in a step, the higher of them, or nothing.
  const def = metricDefinitions.find((d) => d.name === "deploys.confirmed");
  const result = (statistics, total, point) => ({ run: { granularity: M, ...(statistics ? { statistics } : {}) }, calculations: [{ calculation: "count", aggregates: [{ value: 1, ...total }], series: [{ time: "2026-10-11 16:01:00", data: [{ value: 1, ...point }] }] }] });
  const sampled = (...given) => metricSeries(result(...given), def, []).sampled;
  expect([sampled(), sampled({}), sampled({ abr_level: 1 }, { sampleInterval: 1 }, { sampleInterval: 1 }), sampled({ abr_level: 0 }), sampled({ abr_level: null }, { sampleInterval: "x" })]).toEqual([1, 1, 1, 1, 1]);
  expect([sampled({ abr_level: 10 }), sampled(null, { sampleInterval: 10 }), sampled(null, {}, { sampleInterval: 2.5 }), sampled({ abr_level: 10 }, { sampleInterval: 100 }, { sampleInterval: 3 })]).toEqual([10, 10, 2.5, 100]);
  expect([metricSeries(null, def, []).sampled, metricSeries({}, def, []).sampled]).toEqual([1, 1]);
  return "parts and join";
}
// %%
// The memory and the minutes with the time given, so nothing here waits or reads the clock.
test_metric_memory_forgets_at_its_time_and_the_ask_is_cut_to_minutes = {
  const T = 1791676800000, ms = metricMemoryDefaults.ms;
  expect(metricMemoryDefaults).toEqual({ ms: 60000, characters: 4000000 });
  // Kept for `ms` from when it was kept, and not a millisecond more. A memory of this test's own.
  const memory = metricMemoryOf();
  expect(memory.read("a", T, ms)).toBe(null);
  expect(memory.keep("a", "one", T, ms)).toBe(true);
  expect([memory.read("a", T, ms), memory.read("a", T + ms - 1, ms), memory.read("a", T + ms, ms), memory.read("a", T - 1, ms), memory.read("b", T, ms)]).toEqual(["one", "one", null, null, null]);
  // Kept again, it is the later text and the later time.
  expect(memory.keep("a", "two", T + 1000, ms)).toBe(true);
  expect([memory.read("a", T + ms, ms), memory.read("a", T + ms + 1000, ms), memory.held()]).toEqual(["two", null, { answers: 1, characters: 4 }]);
  // With no time to keep it, it is not kept, and what was kept under the key goes.
  for (const none of [0, -1, NaN]) {
    memory.keep("b", "kept", T, ms);
    expect([String(none), memory.keep("b", "not", T, none), memory.read("b", T, ms)]).toEqual([String(none), false, null]);
  }
  // A keep takes out what has passed its time.
  memory.keep("a", "old", T, ms);
  expect(memory.held()).toEqual({ answers: 1, characters: 4 });
  memory.keep("b", "new", T + ms, ms);
  expect([memory.held(), memory.read("a", T + ms, 1e9), memory.read("b", T + ms, ms)]).toEqual([{ answers: 1, characters: 4 }, null, "new"]);
  // The bound is of the keys and the texts together: the oldest goes first, and a text that does not fit alone is not kept.
  const small = metricMemoryOf(30);
  for (const key of ["a", "b", "c"]) expect(small.keep(key, "x".repeat(9), T, ms)).toBe(true);
  expect(small.held()).toEqual({ answers: 3, characters: 30 });
  expect(small.keep("d", "x".repeat(9), T, ms)).toBe(true);
  expect(["a", "b", "c", "d"].map((key) => small.read(key, T, ms) !== null)).toEqual([false, true, true, true]);
  expect(small.keep("e", "x".repeat(19), T, ms)).toBe(true);
  expect([["b", "c", "d", "e"].map((key) => small.read(key, T, ms) !== null), small.held()]).toEqual([[false, false, true, true], { answers: 2, characters: 30 }]);
  expect([small.keep("d", "x".repeat(30), T, ms), small.read("d", T, ms), small.held()]).toEqual([false, null, { answers: 1, characters: 20 }]);
  // The ask: since and until are each cut to the minute they are in; with neither, the hour that ends at the minute of now.
  const def = metricDefinitions.find((d) => d.name === "deploys.confirmed"), M = 60000;
  const asked = (query, now = T + 30 * M + 12345) => { const out = metricAsk(def, new URLSearchParams(query), now); return out.error ? "400" : [out.since - T, out.until - T]; };
  expect(asked("")).toEqual([-30 * M, 30 * M]);
  expect(asked("", T + 30 * M)).toEqual([-30 * M, 30 * M]);
  expect(asked("", T + 31 * M - 1)).toEqual([-30 * M, 30 * M]);
  expect(asked("", T + 31 * M)).toEqual([-29 * M, 31 * M]);
  expect(asked(`since=${T + 1}&until=${T + 10 * M + 59999}`)).toEqual([0, 10 * M]);
  expect(asked(`until=${T + 10 * M + 59999}`)).toEqual([-50 * M, 10 * M]);
  expect(asked(`since=${T + 59999}`)).toEqual([0, 30 * M]);
  expect(asked(`since=${T}&until=${T + M}`)).toEqual([0, M]);
  // One minute after the cut is no span.
  expect(asked(`since=${T}&until=${T + M - 1}`)).toBe("400");
  expect(asked(`since=${T + 30 * M + 1}`)).toBe("400");
  return "kept " + ms + " ms";
}
// %%
test_dashboard_declares_one_cloudflare_permission_and_its_rows = {
  const { meta, parts, source } = await dashboard_service.emit();
  expect(meta.worker).toBe("brain-x-dashboard");
  // The reference the Worker serves holds the first cell with its holes filled: a row a definition, and both rules.
  expect(source.reference.startsWith("# brain-dashboard")).toBe(true);
  for (const d of metricDefinitions) expect(source.reference).toContain("| `" + d.name + "` | `" + d.worker + "` |");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("| `metric.query` | `" + metricRules.query + "` |");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("| `metric.list` | `" + metricRules.list + "` |");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("| `metric.put` | `" + metricRules.put + "` |");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("| `metric.delete` | `" + metricRules.delete + "` |");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("A member keeps " + metricLimits.kept + " metrics.");
  // The dashboards: the four rules, a row a panel of each built-in one, the draws and the limits.
  for (const name of ["list", "get", "put", "delete"]) expect(source.reference).toContain("| `dashboard." + name + "` | `" + dashboardRules[name] + "` |");
  for (const d of dashboardDefinitions) for (const p of d.panels) expect(source.reference).toContain("| `" + d.name + "` | " + d.title + " | " + p.title + " | `" + p.metric + "` | " + p.by.map((k) => "`" + k + "`").join(", ") + " | `" + p.draw + "` |");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("// one of calls, faults, methods, bars, table");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("// 1 to " + dashboardLimits.panels + "\n");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("A caller keeps " + dashboardLimits.kept + " dashboards");
  // Who the service answers: a member's Worker is the member (review 1615), and the reference says so.
  expect(source.reference).toContain("So a member's Worker is answered as the member is: it writes, lists, reads and deletes its author's metrics and dashboards");
  expect(source.reference).not.toContain("a member's Worker included");
  // What a query costs: the memory's time and bound are the module's values, and the shape of cost is named.
  expect(source.reference).toContain("for " + metricMemoryDefaults.ms / 1000 + " s from when Cloudflare answered");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("is over " + metricMemoryDefaults.characters + " characters");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("stands in for the " + metricMemoryDefaults.ms + " ms");
  expect(source.reference).toContain('`cost` is `{ "ms": 0, "queries": 0, "cached": true }`');
  expect(source.reference).toContain("| `{ metric, since, until, step, groups, sampled, series, cost }`");
  expect(source.reference).not.toContain("the memory of an answer and the page");
  // What was counted on cb4 (dsv-4-cost-on-cb4) is said, and the sentences that waited for it are gone.
  // metric-query-sampled-unsaid: the answer says a sample, and the parts' length and count are the module's values.
  expect(source.reference).toContain("An answer says whether Cloudflare made it from a sample of the lines: `sampled`.");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("the span is longer than " + metricPieceDefaults.ms / 3600000 + " hours");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("a span of more than " + metricPieceDefaults.most + " parts");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("or up to " + (1 + metricPieceDefaults.most) + " for a span Cloudflare sampled");
  for (const gone of ["nothing in it says so", "The service does not read whether Cloudflare sampled", "that has to be whole is asked a day at a time"]) expect(source.reference).not.toContain(gone);
  expect(source.reference).toContain("| 24 hours | 854 to 1095 |");
  for (const waited of ["not counted yet", "Whether Cloudflare samples", "and none is kept", "an ask does not wait for another's (read in"]) expect(source.reference).not.toContain(waited);
  expect(source.reference).not.toMatch(/\$\{/);
  expect(meta.cloudflare).toEqual(["Workers Observability Read"]);
  // Rows for a member's definitions, beside the Cloudflare token: the first service with both.
  expect([meta.resources, meta.secrets, meta.calls]).toEqual([["rows"], [], []]);
  // The token is read from the binding the deployer made, and the script filter is brain-logs' own cell, carried into this Worker.
  expect(parts[0].text).toContain("__rt.platform.secrets.CF_TOKEN");
  expect(parts[0].text).toContain("$workers.scriptName");
  expect(parts[0].text).toMatch(/const logsScope = /);
  expect(parts[0].text).toMatch(/const logsScript = /);
  // Every definition is over a Worker of the Brain, with at most 8 dimensions, none of them who called.
  for (const d of metricDefinitions) {
    expect([d.name, logsScript("cb4", d.worker) !== null, d.dims.length <= 8, /^[a-z]+\.[a-z-]+$/.test(d.name)]).toEqual([d.name, true, true, true]);
    expect(d.dims.map((x) => x.key).filter((k) => ["caller", "holder", "delegation", "by", "origin", "via", "ray", "reason"].includes(k))).toEqual([]);
  }
  return meta.cloudflare[0];
}
// %%
import {cloudflare, cloudflareApi, rows, config, simulate, decide, callerOf, sha256} from "@tomlarkworthy/cloudflare-iac"
// %%
import {logsScope, logsScript} from "@tomlarkworthy/brain-logs"
// %%
import {plugins} from "@tomlarkworthy/plugin-registry"
// %%
import {expect} from "@tomlarkworthy/jest-expect-standalone"
